{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjFAEXUMaJLGWRrFnAdS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Sa2j9gh6yU8TeyEbJhQVTv","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223859__x35112d/work/WhiffFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-223859/engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21548,"cache_read_input_tokens":203416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21548},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"74f9e58d-85f9-4ce1-8764-ee4e0d558231","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:42:06.086Z","request_id":"req_011CgjFAEHLebZwhJXtxm59a","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Sa2j9gh6yU8TeyEbJhQVTv":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223859__x35112d/work/WhiffFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-223859/engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Sa2j9gh6yU8TeyEbJhQVTv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Object Studio\n2\t\n3\tObjects (props) are JSON documents of named parts. A command is one line, `tool key=value ...`\n4\tor `{\"tool\":\"…\",\"args\":{…}}`; keep it on that line, document and all: a line break splits it\n5\tinto broken commands.\n6\t\n7\t## The loop\n8\t\n9\t1. `assets find=words` finds a starting point: templates (BUILTIN/box, crate, bench, lantern),\n10\t   library packs (LIB/pack/name, read-only: copy one; imported packs: docs/ASSET_IMPORT.md) and\n11\t   saved objects (WORKSHOP/name). Rows are name cat size_cm tier mesh tok tags desc, best first\n12\t   (tier: standard, checked or disk; mesh: % read-only mesh); a miss says `none` with a route;\n13\t   filters `category=`, `tags=` (`@sit`: a socket), `tier=standard` (what every build has),\n14\t   `similar=NAME`; `next` pages.\n15\t2. Make the object and look at it in one go: a create command like the one below and, on the\n16\t   next line, `asset_preview name=x views=true figure=true`. The create reply has size_cm and\n17\t   check (what is wrong); the preview writes a sheet of four views beside a 1.8 m figure, the\n18\t   image to look at (the reply's path; no capture needed).\n19\t3. If the check or the sheet shows a fault, fix it in one more go: a patch (below) and a new\n20\t   sheet. Otherwise stop; the first go is often the whole job.\n21\t\n22\t## A document\n23\t\n24\t```json\n25\t{\"tool\":\"asset_edit\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"create\",\"name\":\"bench\",\"asset\":{\"format\":2,\"name\":\"bench\",\"unit\":\"cm\",\"description\":\"A wooden bench, its backrest leaning on the rear legs.\",\"materials\":{\"wood\":{\"color\":\"#bc8150\"},\"wood_dark\":{\"color\":\"#594635\"}},\"parts\":{\"seat\":{\"type\":\"rounded_box\",\"size\":[220,18,76],\"radius\":2.5,\"pos\":[0,80,0],\"mat\":\"wood\"},\"backrest\":{\"type\":\"rounded_box\",\"size\":[220,8],\"radius\":2.5,\"from\":[0,92,-38],\"to\":[0,141,-48],\"mat\":\"wood\"},\"leg_front\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[10,8],\"from\":[85,0,25],\"to\":[85,71,25],\"mat\":\"wood_dark\",\"mirror\":\"x\"},\"leg_back\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[10,8],\"from\":[85,1,-26],\"to\":[85,141,-56],\"mat\":\"wood_dark\",\"mirror\":\"x\"},\"crossbar\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[6,6],\"from\":[-80,31,-33],\"to\":[80,31,-33],\"mat\":\"wood_dark\"}},\"sockets\":{\"sit\":{\"pos\":[0,89,4]}}}}}\n26\t```\n27\t\n28\tCentimetres; x right, y up, z forward (+z is the front); the origin is on the floor under the\n29\tcentre. Part names: lowercase letters, digits, _ and -.\n30\t\n31\t- **Place** a part by pos (its centre); by from/to, the visible ends of a box, rounded_box,\n32\t  cylinder, cone, tube or capsule (they set its length: a box takes size [across, thick]); or by\n33\t  attach:\"seat\" (on its top; {\"to\":\"seat\",\"at\":\"front\"}: top, bottom, front, back, left, right)\n34\t  plus offset. yaw, pitch, roll: degrees about y, x, z; +yaw turns +z toward +x, +pitch tips +z\n35\t  down. Round parts stand along y; axis:\"x\" lays one along x.\n36\t- **Shapes** (type; full sizes): box size; rounded_box size, radius (at most half the thinnest\n37\t  side); sphere radius; ellipsoid size; cylinder radius, height; cone radius, radius_end, height;\n38\t  capsule radius, height; tube radius, thickness, height; torus radius, minor_radius; wedge size,\n39\t  peak (-1 back … 1 front, 0 a gable); lathe profile [[r,y],…]; extrude points [[x,y],…],\n40\t  depth. arc (degrees) keeps part of a round shape, its middle toward facing (x, y, z, -x, -y,\n41\t  -z).\n42\t- **Colour.** Each part needs color (#rrggbb or a role: $floor $floor2 $wall $pillar $accent\n43\t  $light) or mat: a key in materials ({color, look, emissive}, or a patterned library material\n44\t  such as \"MAT/oak_planks\"), or a library name itself. Patterns, the library and your own\n45\t  materials: docs/MATERIALS.md. look: cel (default), flat, lit, unlit, cutout. emissive 0-32\n46\t  glows; above 0.5 it lights the room.\n47\t- **Groups.** parts:{…} in a node makes a group: its children sit in its frame and inherit mat,\n48\t  color, look, emissive and solid.\n49\t- **Copies.** mirror:\"x\" (or [\"x\",\"z\"]) adds the reflection; array:{count, step:[x,y,z]} a row;\n50\t  grid:{count:[a,b], step:[sa,sb]} a floor grid (plane:\"xy\": a wall); radial:{count, radius} a\n51\t  ring round the part's position, each copy facing out (axis:\"z\", arc:180, start:-90: an arch).\n52\t  All are centred. cycle goes inside one (array:{count, step, cycle:[\"wood\",\"wood_dark\"]}) and\n53\t  gives copy i entry i mod n. Copies are named leg[0], mirror copies leg~x.\n54\t- **More.** solid:false: not in the collider; hidden:true: collision only. light:{color, radius,\n55\t  intensity} and fx:{preset} (fire, smoke, sparks, embers, steam, magic …) sit at a visible part.\n56\t  chance, jitter and a group's pick:n vary copies by seed. sockets: sit, grip, grip2, tip, top,\n57\t  hang, wall_mount. {\"ref\":\"BUILTIN/crate\",\"pos\":[…],\"scale\":0.5} reuses an asset.\n58\t  {\"mesh\":\"kenney_mini_dungeon/chair\"} is a mesh part `asset_import` wrote: place, scale, mirror,\n59\t  recolor:{\"0\":\"#rrggbb\"} or solid:false it; never edit its file.\n60\t\n61\tLimits: 256 nodes, 1,024 parts after copies, 4 lights, 16 mesh parts. `asset_edit action=schema [topic=node]` is\n62\tthe field guide (also tags, category, spin, sway, segments, half, half_height, remap, source, fit,\n63\tmesh, recolor; material base, roughness, metallic, map, turn, layers).\n64\t\n65\t## Edits\n66\t\n67\t```json\n68\t{\"tool\":\"asset_edit\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"patch\",\"name\":\"x\",\"if_revision\":\"prop2-…\",\"ops\":[{\"op\":\"set\",\"part\":\"seat\",\"fields\":{\"mat\":\"wood_dark\",\"size\":[220,20,76]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"part\":\"arm\",\"value\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[6,20,60],\"pos\":[-104,99,0],\"mat\":\"wood\",\"mirror\":\"x\"}},{\"op\":\"remove\",\"part\":\"crossbar\"}]}}\n69\t```\n70\t\n71\tif_revision is the last reply's revision. Ops target part (roof.slab in a group; parts:[…] for\n72\tseveral), material or socket: set merges fields (\"array.count\":8 reaches in, null deletes); add\n73\ttakes a whole part; also remove, rename, copy (to), mirror, array, expand (copies become parts),\n74\tmove (by), scale (by), unit (to). One bad op rejects the batch; dry_run:true saves nothing; undo,\n75\tredo. create refuses an existing name: action=replace resends a whole document, a patch just\n76\tthe change.\n77\tReplies carry revision, size_cm (width x height x depth), changed_parts and new findings.\n78\taction=inspect returns the document (resolved=true: every part after copies).\n79\t\n80\t## Families (params and presets)\n81\t\n82\t```json\n83\t{\"tool\":\"asset_edit\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"patch\",\"name\":\"fence\",\"ops\":[{\"op\":\"set\",\"fields\":{\"params.length\":{\"range\":[100,300],\"set\":{\"post.pos.0\":0.5,\"rail.size.0\":1}},\"params.pickets\":{\"range\":[3,15],\"int\":true,\"set\":{\"picket.array.count\":1}},\"params.broken\":{\"choices\":[\"no\",\"yes\"],\"set\":{\"picket.chance\":[1,0.6]}},\"presets.long\":{\"length\":300,\"pickets\":13}}}]}}\n84\t```\n85\t\n86\tA range param sets each target to value × factor; a choices param sets each target to that\n87\tchoice's value. The file's own values are the defaults, so a family is still a concrete asset:\n88\ta range's targets must agree on one default (within 0.5 or 0.5%; the check names the factor that\n89\tfits), and the first choice must match what the file writes. Targets are part.field paths\n90\t(group.child.size.1, rail.array.span.0, materials.wood.color), never type, ref, mesh or\n91\tattach.to: attach, mirror, array.span and chance place what depends on a size. At most 8 params,\n92\t8 targets each, 8 choices, 16 presets; a document set (above) adds them.\n93\tPlace or show a variant by preset, knobs over it, or both: `asset_spawn name=x:long\n94\tparams={\"broken\":\"yes\"}`, `asset_preview name=x:low` (params=, seed=), a room's\n95\t`asset = \"LIB/core/x:low\"` with `params = { height = 70 }`. Example:\n96\tdocs/asset_plan/examples/families/fence.f2.json.\n97\t\n98\t**Foundations.** `store/foundations.tsv` names a few standard props per archetype (table, seat,\n99\tbed, barrel, container, crate, light, fire, weapon, tool, stall, shelter, gate, vehicle,\n100\tvegetation) that transform into the rest; `assets shelf=prop` lists them first (LIB/core\n101\tleaves) with their size, knobs and presets. Before making one of these, place a variant: a preset\n102\t(`asset_spawn name=LIB/core/chair:stool`), knob values (`params={\"height\":45}`), a palette for\n103\tits roles (`roles={\"$accent\":\"#2f6fb0\"}`) or a seed. Each row's transforms are tested examples\n104\tand its `why` the technique to copy. Fork one when no knob reaches what you need. A copy of a\n105\tcore asset under its own name (`copy from=LIB/core/table name=table`) is its next revision: it\n106\tkeeps that asset's lineage, so publishing it back adds knobs without making it a fork of itself.\n107\t\n108\t## Check and the rest\n109\t\n110\t`asset_edit action=check name=x [target=WxHxD]` (cm) lists all findings and a cost line. Faults:\n111\tfloating, below_floor, not_grounded, unit_suspect, size, size_band, socket_missing; judge on the\n112\tsheet: poke, hidden, z_fight, mirror, tiny. size_band: an object of a known archetype (the last\n113\tword of its name in store/size_bands.tsv, else its first tag: table, chair, barrel, sword …) far\n114\toutside its real size, e.g. a 32 cm table; the line gives a scale op. socket_missing: a weapon\n115\tneeds grip, a seat (chair, stool, bench, throne) sit. A hang socket hangs the object from it;\n116\twall_mount puts its back (z 0) on the wall. Sheets also take views=[front,top,30], elevation= and tile=.\n117\t`asset_spawn action=add name=x pos=[x,y,z]` places a copy in the world. Saves go to\n118\tassets/props/workshop/name.json; a metre template's copy is in metres: send\n119\t{\"op\":\"unit\",\"to\":\"cm\"} before centimetres. `copy from=X` writes the fork's lineage:\n120\t`\"lineage\":{\"method\":\"edited\",\"origin\":\"import\",\"parents\":[\"X@rev\"],\"license\":\"CC0-1.0\",\"credit\":\"…\"}`,\n121\twith X's origin (`import` for an import, `agent` for own work), licence and credit; edits and\n122\tpublish keep it, a patch cannot set it, and a copy of a format-1 template stays format 1 without one.\n123\t\n124\t## Names and tiers\n125\t\n126\tBUILTIN/name (templates) and LIB/core/name are embedded in every build, the browser's too. A\n127\tshipped pack (`props::store::SHIPPED`, today `kaykit_adventurers`) has its files in every build as\n128\twell, while its rows keep their own tier: game data and rooms may name these and the embedded\n129\tones. Other packs (assets/props/lib/pack/) load on first use in native builds; assets/props/local/ (packs, and WORKSHOP_LOCAL/name copies of their assets) is\n130\tgit-ignored, for sources whose licences forbid sharing. Each pack folder has an index.tsv that\n131\t`assets` reads; `assets reindex=pack` (or `=templates`) rewrites it, keeping its note column.\n132\tA pack's PACK.json holds its licence (lib/ takes CC0 and CC-BY, lib/core CC0 only); reindexing a\n133\tpack rewrites assets/props/CREDITS.md.\n134\t\n135\t`asset_edit action=publish name=x if_revision=R review=\"ok: …\"` puts a workshop asset into LIB/core\n136\tafter you look at its sheet (views=true elevation=game) at revision R. It needs no check findings, a description (≤ 120\n137\tchars), a category, 2-6 tags, references to BUILTIN or LIB/core only, core or inline materials\n138\t(not MAT/workshop/), and at most 400 tokens\n139\t(food, tool, signage), 600 (container, lighting, rock, vegetation), 800 (most) or 2,000 (town,\n140\tdungeon). It writes lib/core/x.json, its index row and a review.tsv line at this revision (an\n141\tedited core asset needs a new review); rebuild to embed it.\n142\t\n143\t## Library assets in game code\n144\t\n145\tA game that keeps its own state draws an asset for a unit or a piece of scenery each frame with\n146\tone call, in its view code while the frame's scene is built (as `pav_view/src/arpg.rs` draws\n147\tShardfall):\n148\t\n149\t```rust\n150\tuse pav_view::assets::{emit_asset, Palette, Placement};\n151\tlet at = Placement::at(unit.pos).yaw(unit.heading_deg).id(unit.id); // .scale(1.5), .rot(quat)\n152\temit_asset(scene, \"BUILTIN/crate\", at, unit.id % 8, &Palette::new())?; // any name assets lists\n153\t```\n154\t\n155\tIt draws what a placed copy draws (parts, glow, lights; not `fx` particles). The seed picks the\n156\tvariant (0 as authored; keep to a few seeds per asset); the palette colours `$roles`\n157\t({\"$wall\":\"#5a6b7c\"}); `id` keeps each unit's outline its own. Unknown names fail with the\n158\tnearest one. Units need no physics: the game owns their positions.\n159\t\n160\tCharacters use sockets through their looks and room data: a biped's\n161\t`weapon = { kind = \"staff\", asset = \"LIB/core/mage_staff\" }` holds the object by its grip socket\n162\t(+y along the weapon; the kind still sets reach and swings), and a room performer with\n163\t`seat = \"<object>\"` sits on that object's sit socket (rooms/library_hall.toml). A room object's\n164\t`patch = [ops]` places a one-off variant of an embedded asset (rooms/limits.toml).\n165\t\n166\tScenery that never moves can instead be baked into the level's static regions\n167\t(`statics::StaticProp`: no entity, one collider box, ~75 B in a snapshot); Shardfall dresses\n168\tits rooms this way from `game/props.toml` (docs/GAME.md, \"Dressing\").\n169\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"03aaac72-17f6-4884-8027-c39649324091","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:42:06.112Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223859__x35112d/work/WhiffFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-223859/engine/docs/ASSET_STUDIO.md","content":"# Object Studio\n\nObjects (props) are JSON documents of named parts. A command is one line, `tool key=value ...`\nor `{\"tool\":\"…\",\"args\":{…}}`; keep it on that line, document and all: a line break splits it\ninto broken commands.\n\n## The loop\n\n1. `assets find=words` finds a starting point: templates (BUILTIN/box, crate, bench, lantern),\n   library packs (LIB/pack/name, read-only: copy one; imported packs: docs/ASSET_IMPORT.md) and\n   saved objects (WORKSHOP/name). Rows are name cat size_cm tier mesh tok tags desc, best first\n   (tier: standard, checked or disk; mesh: % read-only mesh); a miss says `none` with a route;\n   filters `category=`, `tags=` (`@sit`: a socket), `tier=standard` (what every build has),\n   `similar=NAME`; `next` pages.\n2. Make the object and look at it in one go: a create command like the one below and, on the\n   next line, `asset_preview name=x views=true figure=true`. The create reply has size_cm and\n   check (what is wrong); the preview writes a sheet of four views beside a 1.8 m figure, the\n   image to look at (the reply's path; no capture needed).\n3. If the check or the sheet shows a fault, fix it in one more go: a patch (below) and a new\n   sheet. Otherwise stop; the first go is often the whole job.\n\n## A document\n\n```json\n{\"tool\":\"asset_edit\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"create\",\"name\":\"bench\",\"asset\":{\"format\":2,\"name\":\"bench\",\"unit\":\"cm\",\"description\":\"A wooden bench, its backrest leaning on the rear legs.\",\"materials\":{\"wood\":{\"color\":\"#bc8150\"},\"wood_dark\":{\"color\":\"#594635\"}},\"parts\":{\"seat\":{\"type\":\"rounded_box\",\"size\":[220,18,76],\"radius\":2.5,\"pos\":[0,80,0],\"mat\":\"wood\"},\"backrest\":{\"type\":\"rounded_box\",\"size\":[220,8],\"radius\":2.5,\"from\":[0,92,-38],\"to\":[0,141,-48],\"mat\":\"wood\"},\"leg_front\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[10,8],\"from\":[85,0,25],\"to\":[85,71,25],\"mat\":\"wood_dark\",\"mirror\":\"x\"},\"leg_back\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[10,8],\"from\":[85,1,-26],\"to\":[85,141,-56],\"mat\":\"wood_dark\",\"mirror\":\"x\"},\"crossbar\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[6,6],\"from\":[-80,31,-33],\"to\":[80,31,-33],\"mat\":\"wood_dark\"}},\"sockets\":{\"sit\":{\"pos\":[0,89,4]}}}}}\n```\n\nCentimetres; x right, y up, z forward (+z is the front); the origin is on the floor under the\ncentre. Part names: lowercase letters, digits, _ and -.\n\n- **Place** a part by pos (its centre); by from/to, the visible ends of a box, rounded_box,\n  cylinder, cone, tube or capsule (they set its length: a box takes size [across, thick]); or by\n  attach:\"seat\" (on its top; {\"to\":\"seat\",\"at\":\"front\"}: top, bottom, front, back, left, right)\n  plus offset. yaw, pitch, roll: degrees about y, x, z; +yaw turns +z toward +x, +pitch tips +z\n  down. Round parts stand along y; axis:\"x\" lays one along x.\n- **Shapes** (type; full sizes): box size; rounded_box size, radius (at most half the thinnest\n  side); sphere radius; ellipsoid size; cylinder radius, height; cone radius, radius_end, height;\n  capsule radius, height; tube radius, thickness, height; torus radius, minor_radius; wedge size,\n  peak (-1 back … 1 front, 0 a gable); lathe profile [[r,y],…]; extrude points [[x,y],…],\n  depth. arc (degrees) keeps part of a round shape, its middle toward facing (x, y, z, -x, -y,\n  -z).\n- **Colour.** Each part needs color (#rrggbb or a role: $floor $floor2 $wall $pillar $accent\n  $light) or mat: a key in materials ({color, look, emissive}, or a patterned library material\n  such as \"MAT/oak_planks\"), or a library name itself. Patterns, the library and your own\n  materials: docs/MATERIALS.md. look: cel (default), flat, lit, unlit, cutout. emissive 0-32\n  glows; above 0.5 it lights the room.\n- **Groups.** parts:{…} in a node makes a group: its children sit in its frame and inherit mat,\n  color, look, emissive and solid.\n- **Copies.** mirror:\"x\" (or [\"x\",\"z\"]) adds the reflection; array:{count, step:[x,y,z]} a row;\n  grid:{count:[a,b], step:[sa,sb]} a floor grid (plane:\"xy\": a wall); radial:{count, radius} a\n  ring round the part's position, each copy facing out (axis:\"z\", arc:180, start:-90: an arch).\n  All are centred. cycle goes inside one (array:{count, step, cycle:[\"wood\",\"wood_dark\"]}) and\n  gives copy i entry i mod n. Copies are named leg[0], mirror copies leg~x.\n- **More.** solid:false: not in the collider; hidden:true: collision only. light:{color, radius,\n  intensity} and fx:{preset} (fire, smoke, sparks, embers, steam, magic …) sit at a visible part.\n  chance, jitter and a group's pick:n vary copies by seed. sockets: sit, grip, grip2, tip, top,\n  hang, wall_mount. {\"ref\":\"BUILTIN/crate\",\"pos\":[…],\"scale\":0.5} reuses an asset.\n  {\"mesh\":\"kenney_mini_dungeon/chair\"} is a mesh part `asset_import` wrote: place, scale, mirror,\n  recolor:{\"0\":\"#rrggbb\"} or solid:false it; never edit its file.\n\nLimits: 256 nodes, 1,024 parts after copies, 4 lights, 16 mesh parts. `asset_edit action=schema [topic=node]` is\nthe field guide (also tags, category, spin, sway, segments, half, half_height, remap, source, fit,\nmesh, recolor; material base, roughness, metallic, map, turn, layers).\n\n## Edits\n\n```json\n{\"tool\":\"asset_edit\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"patch\",\"name\":\"x\",\"if_revision\":\"prop2-…\",\"ops\":[{\"op\":\"set\",\"part\":\"seat\",\"fields\":{\"mat\":\"wood_dark\",\"size\":[220,20,76]}},{\"op\":\"add\",\"part\":\"arm\",\"value\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[6,20,60],\"pos\":[-104,99,0],\"mat\":\"wood\",\"mirror\":\"x\"}},{\"op\":\"remove\",\"part\":\"crossbar\"}]}}\n```\n\nif_revision is the last reply's revision. Ops target part (roof.slab in a group; parts:[…] for\nseveral), material or socket: set merges fields (\"array.count\":8 reaches in, null deletes); add\ntakes a whole part; also remove, rename, copy (to), mirror, array, expand (copies become parts),\nmove (by), scale (by), unit (to). One bad op rejects the batch; dry_run:true saves nothing; undo,\nredo. create refuses an existing name: action=replace resends a whole document, a patch just\nthe change.\nReplies carry revision, size_cm (width x height x depth), changed_parts and new findings.\naction=inspect returns the document (resolved=true: every part after copies).\n\n## Families (params and presets)\n\n```json\n{\"tool\":\"asset_edit\",\"args\":{\"action\":\"patch\",\"name\":\"fence\",\"ops\":[{\"op\":\"set\",\"fields\":{\"params.length\":{\"range\":[100,300],\"set\":{\"post.pos.0\":0.5,\"rail.size.0\":1}},\"params.pickets\":{\"range\":[3,15],\"int\":true,\"set\":{\"picket.array.count\":1}},\"params.broken\":{\"choices\":[\"no\",\"yes\"],\"set\":{\"picket.chance\":[1,0.6]}},\"presets.long\":{\"length\":300,\"pickets\":13}}}]}}\n```\n\nA range param sets each target to value × factor; a choices param sets each target to that\nchoice's value. The file's own values are the defaults, so a family is still a concrete asset:\na range's targets must agree on one default (within 0.5 or 0.5%; the check names the factor that\nfits), and the first choice must match what the file writes. Targets are part.field paths\n(group.child.size.1, rail.array.span.0, materials.wood.color), never type, ref, mesh or\nattach.to: attach, mirror, array.span and chance place what depends on a size. At most 8 params,\n8 targets each, 8 choices, 16 presets; a document set (above) adds them.\nPlace or show a variant by preset, knobs over it, or both: `asset_spawn name=x:long\nparams={\"broken\":\"yes\"}`, `asset_preview name=x:low` (params=, seed=), a room's\n`asset = \"LIB/core/x:low\"` with `params = { height = 70 }`. Example:\ndocs/asset_plan/examples/families/fence.f2.json.\n\n**Foundations.** `store/foundations.tsv` names a few standard props per archetype (table, seat,\nbed, barrel, container, crate, light, fire, weapon, tool, stall, shelter, gate, vehicle,\nvegetation) that transform into the rest; `assets shelf=prop` lists them first (LIB/core\nleaves) with their size, knobs and presets. Before making one of these, place a variant: a preset\n(`asset_spawn name=LIB/core/chair:stool`), knob values (`params={\"height\":45}`), a palette for\nits roles (`roles={\"$accent\":\"#2f6fb0\"}`) or a seed. Each row's transforms are tested examples\nand its `why` the technique to copy. Fork one when no knob reaches what you need. A copy of a\ncore asset under its own name (`copy from=LIB/core/table name=table`) is its next revision: it\nkeeps that asset's lineage, so publishing it back adds knobs without making it a fork of itself.\n\n## Check and the rest\n\n`asset_edit action=check name=x [target=WxHxD]` (cm) lists all findings and a cost line. Faults:\nfloating, below_floor, not_grounded, unit_suspect, size, size_band, socket_missing; judge on the\nsheet: poke, hidden, z_fight, mirror, tiny. size_band: an object of a known archetype (the last\nword of its name in store/size_bands.tsv, else its first tag: table, chair, barrel, sword …) far\noutside its real size, e.g. a 32 cm table; the line gives a scale op. socket_missing: a weapon\nneeds grip, a seat (chair, stool, bench, throne) sit. A hang socket hangs the object from it;\nwall_mount puts its back (z 0) on the wall. Sheets also take views=[front,top,30], elevation= and tile=.\n`asset_spawn action=add name=x pos=[x,y,z]` places a copy in the world. Saves go to\nassets/props/workshop/name.json; a metre template's copy is in metres: send\n{\"op\":\"unit\",\"to\":\"cm\"} before centimetres. `copy from=X` writes the fork's lineage:\n`\"lineage\":{\"method\":\"edited\",\"origin\":\"import\",\"parents\":[\"X@rev\"],\"license\":\"CC0-1.0\",\"credit\":\"…\"}`,\nwith X's origin (`import` for an import, `agent` for own work), licence and credit; edits and\npublish keep it, a patch cannot set it, and a copy of a format-1 template stays format 1 without one.\n\n## Names and tiers\n\nBUILTIN/name (templates) and LIB/core/name are embedded in every build, the browser's too. A\nshipped pack (`props::store::SHIPPED`, today `kaykit_adventurers`) has its files in every build as\nwell, while its rows keep their own tier: game data and rooms may name these and the embedded\nones. Other packs (assets/props/lib/pack/) load on first use in native builds; assets/props/local/ (packs, and WORKSHOP_LOCAL/name copies of their assets) is\ngit-ignored, for sources whose licences forbid sharing. Each pack folder has an index.tsv that\n`assets` reads; `assets reindex=pack` (or `=templates`) rewrites it, keeping its note column.\nA pack's PACK.json holds its licence (lib/ takes CC0 and CC-BY, lib/core CC0 only); reindexing a\npack rewrites assets/props/CREDITS.md.\n\n`asset_edit action=publish name=x if_revision=R review=\"ok: …\"` puts a workshop asset into LIB/core\nafter you look at its sheet (views=true elevation=game) at revision R. It needs no check findings, a description (≤ 120\nchars), a category, 2-6 tags, references to BUILTIN or LIB/core only, core or inline materials\n(not MAT/workshop/), and at most 400 tokens\n(food, tool, signage), 600 (container, lighting, rock, vegetation), 800 (most) or 2,000 (town,\ndungeon). It writes lib/core/x.json, its index row and a review.tsv line at this revision (an\nedited core asset needs a new review); rebuild to embed it.\n\n## Library assets in game code\n\nA game that keeps its own state draws an asset for a unit or a piece of scenery each frame with\none call, in its view code while the frame's scene is built (as `pav_view/src/arpg.rs` draws\nShardfall):\n\n```rust\nuse pav_view::assets::{emit_asset, Palette, Placement};\nlet at = Placement::at(unit.pos).yaw(unit.heading_deg).id(unit.id); // .scale(1.5), .rot(quat)\nemit_asset(scene, \"BUILTIN/crate\", at, unit.id % 8, &Palette::new())?; // any name assets lists\n```\n\nIt draws what a placed copy draws (parts, glow, lights; not `fx` particles). The seed picks the\nvariant (0 as authored; keep to a few seeds per asset); the palette colours `$roles`\n({\"$wall\":\"#5a6b7c\"}); `id` keeps each unit's outline its own. Unknown names fail with the\nnearest one. Units need no physics: the game owns their positions.\n\nCharacters use sockets through their looks and room data: a biped's\n`weapon = { kind = \"staff\", asset = \"LIB/core/mage_staff\" }` holds the object by its grip socket\n(+y along the weapon; the kind still sets reach and swings), and a room performer with\n`seat = \"<object>\"` sits on that object's sit socket (rooms/library_hall.toml). A room object's\n`patch = [ops]` places a one-off variant of an embedded asset (rooms/limits.toml).\n\nScenery that never moves can instead be baked into the level's static regions\n(`statics::StaticProp`: no entity, one collider box, ~75 B in a snapshot); Shardfall dresses\nits rooms this way from `game/props.toml` (docs/GAME.md, \"Dressing\").\n","numLines":169,"startLine":1,"totalLines":169}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Sa2j9gh6yU8TeyEbJhQVTv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjFAEXUMaJLGWRrFnAdS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01E9VDxUXYEhx16j79Lzu1tH","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223859__x35112d/work/WhiffFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-223859/engine/rooms/_template.toml","limit":135,"offset":40},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21548,"cache_read_input_tokens":203416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21548},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"02150af1-9c6a-4297-907e-25073ff9ab6f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:42:08.384Z","request_id":"req_011CgjFAEHLebZwhJXtxm59a","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01E9VDxUXYEhx16j79Lzu1tH":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223859__x35112d/work/WhiffFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-223859/engine/rooms/_template.toml","limit":135,"offset":40}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E9VDxUXYEhx16j79Lzu1tH","type":"tool_result","content":"40\t# Optional: view settings while inside (`pav params prefix=view`, without \"view.\"), e.g. night:\n41\t# \"light.sun_intensity\" = 0.06, \"light.ambient\" = 0.25, sky = \"#0e1424\", bloom = 0.6, gi = 1.0,\n42\t# \"light.sun_elevation\" = 20, distortion = true, particles = true, exposure = 1.2\n43\t# Filters can aim at a part of the scene: \"filter.pixel_target\" = \"objects\" (characters & objects)\n44\t# or \"environment\", \"filter.color_on\" / \"grade_on\" / \"scanlines_on\" / \"grain_on\" / \"chroma_on\",\n45\t# outlines_on = \"objects\", style_objects = \"lit\", style_environment = \"flat\" (see rooms/mix_match.toml)\n46\t# Painterly and print styles: \"filter.stylize\" = \"paint\" | \"halftone\" | \"ascii\" | \"sketch\",\n47\t# \"filter.stylize_on\", \"filter.stylize_size\" (px), \"filter.stylize_color\" (rooms/paint_print.toml).\n48\t# Hazy air: haze, haze_height, shafts, shafts_forward, halos (rooms/light_shafts.toml).\n49\t# Wind and water: wind, wind_angle, wind_gusts, grass_push, water_ripples, water_speed,\n50\t# water_fade, water_rain (rooms/wind_water.toml). Transitions: \"filter.transition\" = \"iris\",\n51\t# \"filter.transition_demo\" = true loops it (rooms/transitions.toml).\n52\t# Rooms without roofs can keep tall things whole near the player: \"cutaway.height_cut\" = false\n53\t[view]\n54\t\n55\t# Optional: simulation parameter overrides while inside (full paths, see `pav params`).\n56\t[params]\n57\t# \"movement.jump_height\" = 2.0\n58\t# \"movement.ledge_grab\" = true     # off by default: a jump reaches ledges up to ~3.4 m, so keep\n59\t#                                   # walls you must not climb at 4 m or more in such rooms\n60\t# \"movement.lock_axis\" = \"z\"       # side-view rooms (axis in the room's own frame)\n61\t\n62\t# Optional: keyboard remapping while inside (action = [physical key names]).\n63\t[keys]\n64\t# jump = [\"KeyW\", \"Space\"]\n65\t# move_up = [\"ArrowUp\"]\n66\t\n67\t[layout]\n68\t# origin is only used when the room is loaded on its own (`pav load scene=<key>`).\n69\torigin = [-5.0, 0.0, -5.0]\n70\t\n71\t[[layout.layer]]\n72\ty = 0                         # more layers = more floors (add at = [col, row] to offset one)\n73\tmap = '''\n74\t###########\n75\t#.........#\n76\t#....B....#\n77\t#.........#\n78\t#.........#\n79\t#.........#\n80\t#.........#\n81\t#.........#\n82\t#.........#\n83\t#####..####\n84\t'''\n85\t\n86\t# Each map character: blocks (y0/y1 relative to the layer), ladder, prop or marker.\n87\t[layout.legend.'.']\n88\tblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }]\n89\t\n90\t[layout.legend.'#']\n91\tblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 2.0, color = \"#9aa5b1\" }]\n92\t\n93\t[layout.legend.'B']\n94\tblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 1.0, color = \"#c9a27a\", rounded = true }]\n95\t# Other options: destructible = true, ghost = true (no collision), inset = 0.3 (thinner),\n96\t# crumble = 0.8 (falls 0.8 s after being stepped on), regrow = 4 (comes back after 4 s),\n97\t# strength = 40 (breaks when hit with more than this contact force, e.g. glass),\n98\t# look = \"flat\" | \"cel\" | \"lit\" | \"unlit\",\n99\t# ladder = { facing = \"north\", height = 3.0 },\n100\t# prop = { shape = { type = \"box\", half = [0.35, 0.35, 0.35] }, color = \"#e8704a\" },\n101\t# marker = \"player\"\n102\t# label = { text = \"HELLO\", size = 0.5, color = \"#2b2d35\", mode = \"floor\" }   (text on the tile)\n103\t# grass = { density = 4, height = 0.55, color = \"#7cbf5a\" }   tufts per cell that sway in the wind\n104\t#                   and part around the player (drawing only)\n105\t# prop = { ..., sway = \"leaves\" }   props (and [[object]]s) can sway: \"leaves\" | \"grass\"\n106\t#\n107\t# zone = { kind = \"...\", ... } makes the tile a trigger (identical neighbours merge):\n108\t#   kind = \"start\" | \"finish\" | \"gate\" | \"checkpoint\" | \"kill\" | \"water\" | \"pad\" | \"camera\" |\n109\t#          \"conveyor\" (facing = direction, speed = m/s; carries characters and props) |\n110\t#          \"bounce\" (speed = launch m/s; trampolines for characters and props)\n111\t#   course = \"name\"   start/finish/gates of one course share it; leaving START starts the timer,\n112\t#                     gates must be passed in `index` order (missed gate = +2 s), FINISH stops it\n113\t#   index = 1         gate order\n114\t#   y0 = 0, y1 = 3    height range relative to the layer (kill zones in pits: e.g. y0 = -3, y1 = -1)\n115\t#   label = \"TEXT\"    drawn on the floor (label_size = 0.5 to override the auto fit);\n116\t#                     color = \"#rrggbb\" or \"none\"; facing = \"east\" (respawn direction)\n117\t#   Zones are half-open boxes, so touching zones never overlap. A respawn point that lies in a\n118\t#   zone does not trigger it (respawning onto START keeps the timer running).\n119\t#   params = { \"movement.model\" = \"momentum\" }       pads: parameter changes until you leave\n120\t#                     (\"view.bloom\" = 1.5 etc. change view settings the same way)\n121\t#   signal = \"drop\"   pads: tells spawners listening for \"drop\" to fire\n122\t#   note = \"...\"      pads: what it sets and what to look for (on screen while you stand on it;\n123\t#                     required on every pad with params)\n124\t#   camera = { set = { tilt = 90, ortho = true }, sweep = [{ param = \"tilt\", from = 90,\n125\t#              to = 10, period = 12 }], flip_ortho = 6 }  pads (sticky) / camera zones (inside)\n126\t#   water: swim below y1 (its surface ripples: a CPU wave simulation; neighbouring water tiles\n127\t#   with the same top that form a rectangle ripple as one surface). kill: back to the last checkpoint.\n128\t\n129\t# Free text anywhere (layout space: x = column, y = height, z = row).\n130\t# [[label]]\n131\t# text = \"SIGN\"\n132\t# pos = [5.0, 0.03, 3.0]\n133\t# size = 0.6\n134\t# mode = \"floor\"            # floor (turns to the camera) | wall (faces `facing`) | billboard\n135\t# facing = \"south\"\n136\t\n137\t# Free-placed objects (keep them at the end of the file; edit mode rewrites this part).\n138\t[[object]]\n139\tname = \"ball\"\n140\tshape = { type = \"sphere\", radius = 0.4 }\n141\tpos = [3.5, 1.0, 3.5]           # x = column, y = height, z = row\n142\tcolor = \"#5b8def\"\n143\tbody = \"dynamic\"                # dynamic | fixed | kinematic | none\n144\t\n145\t# Animated objects use body = \"kinematic\" and a behavior (vectors are in the object's own frame):\n146\t#   behavior = { type = \"move\", offset = [0, 0, 4], period = 4, phase = 0, hold = 0.3, smooth = true }\n147\t#     (hold = share of the cycle spent waiting, split between both ends)\n148\t#   behavior = { type = \"rotate\", axis = [0, 1, 0], speed = 90 }                   (deg/s)\n149\t#   behavior = { type = \"rotate\", axis = [1, 0, 0], swing = 60, period = 2, pivot = [0, 2, 0] }\n150\t#   behavior = { type = \"spin\", speed = 1.5 }                                       (rad/s)\n151\t# Projectile emitters (body = \"none\", or \"fixed\" with a slim shape; bullets ignore their emitter):\n152\t#   behavior = { type = \"emitter\", pattern = \"aimed\", interval = 1.0, count = 1, spread = 0,\n153\t#                speed = 6, radius = 0.15, height = 0, range = 30, delay = 0, burst = 0, pause = 1,\n154\t#                color = \"#ff5a3c\", knockback = 6, gravity = 0, spin = 12, life = 6 }\n155\t#     pattern: aimed (at the player) | forward (+Z of the object, see yaw) | ring | spiral | random\n156\t# Touching a hazard knocks you back (respawn = true sends you to the last checkpoint):\n157\t#   hazard = { knockback = 7, respawn = false }\n158\t# Spawners drop props on a timer and/or when a pad sends their signal (body = \"none\"):\n159\t#   behavior = { type = \"spawner\", shape = { type = \"box\", half = [0.3, 0.3, 0.3] }, color = \"\",\n160\t#                count = 20, interval = 0, max = 200, area = [1.5, 0.5, 1.5], signal = \"drop\",\n161\t#                clear = \"clear\", density = 1, friction = 0.5, restitution = 0.1, tumble = true }\n162\t#     (pending = 1 drops one batch on the first tick, so the room starts with its props)\n163\t# The store's catalogue (rooms/catalogue.toml; body = \"none\"): a pad's signal lays out the next\n164\t# page of the store's object rows (embedded, then the committed packs on disk, then the shipped\n165\t# packs the disk lacks), each beside a 1.8 m figure with its row; `back` pages back; toward = -1\n166\t# grows the page toward -z with its first line at the object (put it by the pads):\n167\t#   behavior = { type = \"catalogue\", signal = \"next\", back = \"back\", per_page = 20, columns = 5 }\n168\t# The clip browser (rooms/clip_browser.toml; body = \"none\"): every [[npc]] whose name starts with\n169\t# `cast` plays the same clip; pads step through the library, jump to a set's first clip or toggle\n170\t# auto-play, and the clip's card lies on the floor at the object:\n171\t#   behavior = { type = \"clip_browser\", next = \"clip_next\", back = \"clip_back\", auto = \"clip_auto\",\n172\t#                cast = \"cast\", hold = 5, start = \"QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop\",\n173\t#                sets = [[\"clip_set_cmu\", \"CMU\"], [\"clip_set_quaternius\", \"QUATERNIUS\"]] }\n174\t# An imported figure (a shipped pack's, e.g. LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight) can wear any biped"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"0fea3637-13e3-48d1-9ae9-c250cb325091","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:42:08.397Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223859__x35112d/work/WhiffFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-223859/engine/rooms/_template.toml","content":"# Optional: view settings while inside (`pav params prefix=view`, without \"view.\"), e.g. night:\n# \"light.sun_intensity\" = 0.06, \"light.ambient\" = 0.25, sky = \"#0e1424\", bloom = 0.6, gi = 1.0,\n# \"light.sun_elevation\" = 20, distortion = true, particles = true, exposure = 1.2\n# Filters can aim at a part of the scene: \"filter.pixel_target\" = \"objects\" (characters & objects)\n# or \"environment\", \"filter.color_on\" / \"grade_on\" / \"scanlines_on\" / \"grain_on\" / \"chroma_on\",\n# outlines_on = \"objects\", style_objects = \"lit\", style_environment = \"flat\" (see rooms/mix_match.toml)\n# Painterly and print styles: \"filter.stylize\" = \"paint\" | \"halftone\" | \"ascii\" | \"sketch\",\n# \"filter.stylize_on\", \"filter.stylize_size\" (px), \"filter.stylize_color\" (rooms/paint_print.toml).\n# Hazy air: haze, haze_height, shafts, shafts_forward, halos (rooms/light_shafts.toml).\n# Wind and water: wind, wind_angle, wind_gusts, grass_push, water_ripples, water_speed,\n# water_fade, water_rain (rooms/wind_water.toml). Transitions: \"filter.transition\" = \"iris\",\n# \"filter.transition_demo\" = true loops it (rooms/transitions.toml).\n# Rooms without roofs can keep tall things whole near the player: \"cutaway.height_cut\" = false\n[view]\n\n# Optional: simulation parameter overrides while inside (full paths, see `pav params`).\n[params]\n# \"movement.jump_height\" = 2.0\n# \"movement.ledge_grab\" = true     # off by default: a jump reaches ledges up to ~3.4 m, so keep\n#                                   # walls you must not climb at 4 m or more in such rooms\n# \"movement.lock_axis\" = \"z\"       # side-view rooms (axis in the room's own frame)\n\n# Optional: keyboard remapping while inside (action = [physical key names]).\n[keys]\n# jump = [\"KeyW\", \"Space\"]\n# move_up = [\"ArrowUp\"]\n\n[layout]\n# origin is only used when the room is loaded on its own (`pav load scene=<key>`).\norigin = [-5.0, 0.0, -5.0]\n\n[[layout.layer]]\ny = 0                         # more layers = more floors (add at = [col, row] to offset one)\nmap = '''\n###########\n#.........#\n#....B....#\n#.........#\n#.........#\n#.........#\n#.........#\n#.........#\n#.........#\n#####..####\n'''\n\n# Each map character: blocks (y0/y1 relative to the layer), ladder, prop or marker.\n[layout.legend.'.']\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }]\n\n[layout.legend.'#']\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 2.0, color = \"#9aa5b1\" }]\n\n[layout.legend.'B']\nblocks = [{ y0 = -0.5, y1 = 0, color = \"#c8c8c8\" }, { y0 = 0, y1 = 1.0, color = \"#c9a27a\", rounded = true }]\n# Other options: destructible = true, ghost = true (no collision), inset = 0.3 (thinner),\n# crumble = 0.8 (falls 0.8 s after being stepped on), regrow = 4 (comes back after 4 s),\n# strength = 40 (breaks when hit with more than this contact force, e.g. glass),\n# look = \"flat\" | \"cel\" | \"lit\" | \"unlit\",\n# ladder = { facing = \"north\", height = 3.0 },\n# prop = { shape = { type = \"box\", half = [0.35, 0.35, 0.35] }, color = \"#e8704a\" },\n# marker = \"player\"\n# label = { text = \"HELLO\", size = 0.5, color = \"#2b2d35\", mode = \"floor\" }   (text on the tile)\n# grass = { density = 4, height = 0.55, color = \"#7cbf5a\" }   tufts per cell that sway in the wind\n#                   and part around the player (drawing only)\n# prop = { ..., sway = \"leaves\" }   props (and [[object]]s) can sway: \"leaves\" | \"grass\"\n#\n# zone = { kind = \"...\", ... } makes the tile a trigger (identical neighbours merge):\n#   kind = \"start\" | \"finish\" | \"gate\" | \"checkpoint\" | \"kill\" | \"water\" | \"pad\" | \"camera\" |\n#          \"conveyor\" (facing = direction, speed = m/s; carries characters and props) |\n#          \"bounce\" (speed = launch m/s; trampolines for characters and props)\n#   course = \"name\"   start/finish/gates of one course share it; leaving START starts the timer,\n#                     gates must be passed in `index` order (missed gate = +2 s), FINISH stops it\n#   index = 1         gate order\n#   y0 = 0, y1 = 3    height range relative to the layer (kill zones in pits: e.g. y0 = -3, y1 = -1)\n#   label = \"TEXT\"    drawn on the floor (label_size = 0.5 to override the auto fit);\n#                     color = \"#rrggbb\" or \"none\"; facing = \"east\" (respawn direction)\n#   Zones are half-open boxes, so touching zones never overlap. A respawn point that lies in a\n#   zone does not trigger it (respawning onto START keeps the timer running).\n#   params = { \"movement.model\" = \"momentum\" }       pads: parameter changes until you leave\n#                     (\"view.bloom\" = 1.5 etc. change view settings the same way)\n#   signal = \"drop\"   pads: tells spawners listening for \"drop\" to fire\n#   note = \"...\"      pads: what it sets and what to look for (on screen while you stand on it;\n#                     required on every pad with params)\n#   camera = { set = { tilt = 90, ortho = true }, sweep = [{ param = \"tilt\", from = 90,\n#              to = 10, period = 12 }], flip_ortho = 6 }  pads (sticky) / camera zones (inside)\n#   water: swim below y1 (its surface ripples: a CPU wave simulation; neighbouring water tiles\n#   with the same top that form a rectangle ripple as one surface). kill: back to the last checkpoint.\n\n# Free text anywhere (layout space: x = column, y = height, z = row).\n# [[label]]\n# text = \"SIGN\"\n# pos = [5.0, 0.03, 3.0]\n# size = 0.6\n# mode = \"floor\"            # floor (turns to the camera) | wall (faces `facing`) | billboard\n# facing = \"south\"\n\n# Free-placed objects (keep them at the end of the file; edit mode rewrites this part).\n[[object]]\nname = \"ball\"\nshape = { type = \"sphere\", radius = 0.4 }\npos = [3.5, 1.0, 3.5]           # x = column, y = height, z = row\ncolor = \"#5b8def\"\nbody = \"dynamic\"                # dynamic | fixed | kinematic | none\n\n# Animated objects use body = \"kinematic\" and a behavior (vectors are in the object's own frame):\n#   behavior = { type = \"move\", offset = [0, 0, 4], period = 4, phase = 0, hold = 0.3, smooth = true }\n#     (hold = share of the cycle spent waiting, split between both ends)\n#   behavior = { type = \"rotate\", axis = [0, 1, 0], speed = 90 }                   (deg/s)\n#   behavior = { type = \"rotate\", axis = [1, 0, 0], swing = 60, period = 2, pivot = [0, 2, 0] }\n#   behavior = { type = \"spin\", speed = 1.5 }                                       (rad/s)\n# Projectile emitters (body = \"none\", or \"fixed\" with a slim shape; bullets ignore their emitter):\n#   behavior = { type = \"emitter\", pattern = \"aimed\", interval = 1.0, count = 1, spread = 0,\n#                speed = 6, radius = 0.15, height = 0, range = 30, delay = 0, burst = 0, pause = 1,\n#                color = \"#ff5a3c\", knockback = 6, gravity = 0, spin = 12, life = 6 }\n#     pattern: aimed (at the player) | forward (+Z of the object, see yaw) | ring | spiral | random\n# Touching a hazard knocks you back (respawn = true sends you to the last checkpoint):\n#   hazard = { knockback = 7, respawn = false }\n# Spawners drop props on a timer and/or when a pad sends their signal (body = \"none\"):\n#   behavior = { type = \"spawner\", shape = { type = \"box\", half = [0.3, 0.3, 0.3] }, color = \"\",\n#                count = 20, interval = 0, max = 200, area = [1.5, 0.5, 1.5], signal = \"drop\",\n#                clear = \"clear\", density = 1, friction = 0.5, restitution = 0.1, tumble = true }\n#     (pending = 1 drops one batch on the first tick, so the room starts with its props)\n# The store's catalogue (rooms/catalogue.toml; body = \"none\"): a pad's signal lays out the next\n# page of the store's object rows (embedded, then the committed packs on disk, then the shipped\n# packs the disk lacks), each beside a 1.8 m figure with its row; `back` pages back; toward = -1\n# grows the page toward -z with its first line at the object (put it by the pads):\n#   behavior = { type = \"catalogue\", signal = \"next\", back = \"back\", per_page = 20, columns = 5 }\n# The clip browser (rooms/clip_browser.toml; body = \"none\"): every [[npc]] whose name starts with\n# `cast` plays the same clip; pads step through the library, jump to a set's first clip or toggle\n# auto-play, and the clip's card lies on the floor at the object:\n#   behavior = { type = \"clip_browser\", next = \"clip_next\", back = \"clip_back\", auto = \"clip_auto\",\n#                cast = \"cast\", hold = 5, start = \"QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop\",\n#                sets = [[\"clip_set_cmu\", \"CMU\"], [\"clip_set_quaternius\", \"QUATERNIUS\"]] }\n# An imported figure (a shipped pack's, e.g. LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight) can wear any biped","numLines":135,"startLine":40,"totalLines":282}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E9VDxUXYEhx16j79Lzu1tH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjFAEXUMaJLGWRrFnAdS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Vwg86QVs3fM4fRVoDsyXtf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 163,260p rooms/_template.toml; grep -n \"pub struct CameraParams\" -A22 crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs; grep -n \"pub fn \" crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs | head -30; sed -n 715,800p crates/pav_view/src/build.rs; sed -n 1,40p crates/pav_app/src/uiinput.rs; ls engine 2>/dev/null; ls assets/props/lib/core | head -30; ls assets/props/lib/core | wc -l; cat assets/props/lib/core/rowboat.json | head -60","description":"Read object fields, camera params, fx events and an example prop"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21548,"cache_read_input_tokens":203416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21548},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"c9b1eafd-6b8d-444f-8f2b-e68c696a92fe","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:42:10.351Z","request_id":"req_011CgjFAEHLebZwhJXtxm59a","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Vwg86QVs3fM4fRVoDsyXtf":{"command":"sed -n 163,260p rooms/_template.toml; grep -n \"pub struct CameraParams\" -A22 crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs; grep -n \"pub fn \" crates/pav_view/src/camera.rs | head -30; sed -n 715,800p crates/pav_view/src/build.rs; sed -n 1,40p crates/pav_app/src/uiinput.rs; ls engine 2>/dev/null; ls assets/props/lib/core | head -30; ls assets/props/lib/core | wc -l; cat assets/props/lib/core/rowboat.json | head -60","description":"Read object fields, camera params, fx events and an example prop"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Vwg86QVs3fM4fRVoDsyXtf","type":"tool_result","content":"# The store's catalogue (rooms/catalogue.toml; body = \"none\"): a pad's signal lays out the next\n# page of the store's object rows (embedded, then the committed packs on disk, then the shipped\n# packs the disk lacks), each beside a 1.8 m figure with its row; `back` pages back; toward = -1\n# grows the page toward -z with its first line at the object (put it by the pads):\n#   behavior = { type = \"catalogue\", signal = \"next\", back = \"back\", per_page = 20, columns = 5 }\n# The clip browser (rooms/clip_browser.toml; body = \"none\"): every [[npc]] whose name starts with\n# `cast` plays the same clip; pads step through the library, jump to a set's first clip or toggle\n# auto-play, and the clip's card lies on the floor at the object:\n#   behavior = { type = \"clip_browser\", next = \"clip_next\", back = \"clip_back\", auto = \"clip_auto\",\n#                cast = \"cast\", hold = 5, start = \"QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop\",\n#                sets = [[\"clip_set_cmu\", \"CMU\"], [\"clip_set_quaternius\", \"QUATERNIUS\"]] }\n# An imported figure (a shipped pack's, e.g. LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight) can wear any biped\n# [[npc]]: look = { figure = \"LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight\" }.\n# More object fields: pitch = 20, roll = 0 (tilt in degrees, e.g. ramps), density = 1 (kg/m³:\n# 1 is very light; 50-100 = pushable crates; 400 = wood; 2000 = stone), friction = 0.5,\n# restitution = 0.0 (bounciness 0..1; rapier averages it with the surface underneath),\n# damping = 0 (air drag). Pushing shares momentum: a 70 kg character barely moves 300 kg.\n# Reusable props made in the Object Studio replace shape and colour:\n#   asset = \"BUILTIN/bench\", scale = 1, body = \"fixed\" (or \"none\": no collision),\n#   seed = 3 (a variant: chance, jitter and pick; 0 as authored),\n#   roles = { \"$wall\" = \"#5a6b7c\" } (colours for the theme roles its parts name),\n#   patch = [{ op = \"scale\", by = 0.5 }] (asset_edit patch ops on this copy only: a one-off\n#   variant, such as a defect on show in rooms/limits.toml; publish variants rooms reuse).\n#   `room_check` names any asset the library does not have, or a patch that does not apply.\n# Visual-only effects on any object (never affect the simulation; body = \"none\" for invisible\n# emitters with a tiny sphere shape):\n#   light = { color = \"#ffb060\", radius = 7, intensity = 2.5, flicker = 0.8, pulse = 0,\n#             shadows = true, offset = [0, 0.7, 0] }   (the 4 shadow-casting lights nearest you)\n#   particles = { preset = \"fire\", rate = 0, color = \"\", size = 1, speed = 1, life = 1,\n#                 area = [0, 0, 0], offset = [0, 0.5, 0] }\n#     presets: fire smoke sparks embers fountain snow rain fireflies magic steam dust bubbles\n#     confetti (rate 0 = the preset's; area = spawn box half-size; snow/rain: put it up high and\n#     set ground = -height so drops land on the floor)\n#   distortion = { kind = \"haze\", radius = 1.5, strength = 0.4, period = 1.5, offset = [0, 1, 0] }\n#     (strength 0.3-0.6 reads at the default camera; 1+ melts the picture)\n#     kinds: haze (heat shimmer) | lens (magnify; negative strength shrinks) | ripple | ring\n#     (a shockwave every `period` s). Bombs make shockwaves, sparks and smoke by themselves.\n#   emissive = 2..8 makes an object glow (bloom) and light its surroundings.\n#   sway = \"leaves\" moves it in the wind (canopies, banners; drawing only), \"grass\" draws a tuft.\n# Drivable vehicles (E to get in / out; jump = handbrake / climb, crouch = brake / descend):\n#   vehicle = { kind = \"car\" }   or   vehicle = { kind = \"helicopter\" }\n#   optional: color, accent, size = [half x, y, z], mass, power, max_speed, grip, drift_grip\n#   (rear grip with the handbrake: low = big drifts), steer (deg), climb (helicopter m/s),\n#   ceiling (helicopter: highest flying height above its pad, m; default 14).\n#   `pos` is where it stands; shape/body come from the vehicle. Courses and checkpoints work\n#   while driving (you respawn in the vehicle).\n# Shootable things (bullet hell, targets): the player shoots with the blaster\n# ([params] \"bombs.weapon\" = \"blaster\", \"bombs.fire_interval\" = 0.1, \"bombs.shoot_angle\" = 180\n# for always-north in this file's map (it turns with the room), -1 = at the cursor;\n# \"bombs.shot_range\" = 35 m; \"movement.hitbox\" = 0.12 for a tiny hitbox). Shots fly about\n# 1.1 m above the floor and hit what they touch in 3D, so put targets near that height:\n#   health = { hp = 40, score = 100, signal = \"boss_dead\", finish = true, bar = true,\n#              sway = [3, 5], phases = [{ below = 0.5, behavior = { type = \"emitter\", ... } }] }\n#   (finish: destroying it finishes the running course; bar: boss health bar; sway: drift\n#   amplitude (m) / period (s) along the object's X; phases: new behaviour below a health\n#   fraction). Score adds to the running course and shows in the HUD. A `finish` boss can\n#   stand in for the course's FINISH tile.\n# Soft (deformable) objects ignore `shape`:\n#   soft = { shape = { type = \"cuboid\", half = [0.6, 0.6, 0.6], res = [4, 4, 4] }, stiffness = 6 }\n#   soft = { shape = { type = \"sphere\", radius = 0.6, subdivisions = 2 }, stiffness = 10 }\n#   soft = { shape = { type = \"cloth\", size = [2, 1.5], res = [10, 8], vertical = true },\n#            pin = \"top\", stiffness = 20 }          (vertical = hangs down from pos, else flat +Z)\n#   soft = { shape = { type = \"rope\", to = [0, -3, 0], segments = 16, radius = 0.05 },\n#            pin = \"start\", attach = \"ball\" }        (rope end tied to the object named \"ball\")\n#   also: damping = 0.3, mass = 4 (kg), tear = 0.6 (breaks when stretched 60%),\n#         pin = \"\" | \"top\" | \"start\" | \"end\" | \"ends\" | \"corners\" | \"top_corners\" | \"edge\"\n\n# Joints between named objects (b = \"\" fixes `a` to the world); `at` = anchor, layout space:\n# [[joint]]\n# a = \"door\"\n# b = \"\"\n# at = [3.0, 1.0, 2.0]\n# joint = { type = \"hinge\", axis = [0, 1, 0], limits = [-90, 90] }\n#   joint types: fixed | ball | hinge (axis, limits deg, motor_speed deg/s, motor_force, or\n#   spring + damping to swing back: self-closing doors) | slider (axis, limits m, spring, damping)\n#   | rope (length) | spring (length, stiffness, damping)\n#   Joints to the world measure the object: a vertical slider's limits = [-1, 0.25] travel 1 m\n#   down and 0.25 m up. at_b = [x, y, z] puts b's (or the world's) anchor elsewhere, e.g. a\n#   spring that starts stretched. Keep chain/joint parts a few cm clear of fixed colliders.\n\n# Generated chains and rope bridges (layout space; density defaults to 400):\n# [[chain]]\n# from = [3.0, 4.0, 2.0]\n# to = [3.0, 1.0, 2.0]\n# links = 8\n# radius = 0.07\n# attach_to = \"ball\"          # tie the end to an object (fix_to = true pins it to the world)\n# [[chain]]\n# style = \"bridge\"            # planks hinged edge to edge, both ends fixed\n# from = [2.0, 0.0, 8.5]\n# to = [14.0, 0.0, 8.5]\n# links = 12\n# width = 1.4\n# sag = 0.04                  # hangs 4% of the span lower in the middle\n# damping = 0.3               # air drag on the links (default 0.3); fewer, longer planks are calmer\n\n# Characters and creatures (layout space). kind = biped | spider | lizard | beetle | blob;\n# ai = idle | wander (radius, pause = [min, max]) | patrol (points = [[x, z], ...], pause) |\n10:pub struct CameraParams {\n11-    /// Degrees above the horizon: 90 = straight down, 0 = side view.\n12-    pub tilt: f32,\n13-    /// Degrees; 0 = looking north (-Z).\n14-    pub yaw: f32,\n15-    /// Distance from the focus point (metres). In orthographic mode it sets the zoom.\n16-    pub distance: f32,\n17-    /// Vertical field of view (degrees). Orthographic uses it to match framing.\n18-    pub fov: f32,\n19-    pub ortho: bool,\n20-    /// Seconds for the camera to catch up with the focus (0 = locked).\n21-    pub follow_lag: f32,\n22-    /// Look slightly above the focus point (metres).\n23-    pub height_offset: f32,\n24-}\n25-\n26-impl Default for CameraParams {\n27-    fn default() -> Self {\n28-        Self { tilt: 62.0, yaw: 0.0, distance: 18.0, fov: 40.0, ortho: false, follow_lag: 0.12, height_offset: 0.8 }\n29-    }\n30-}\n31-\n32-impl Tunable for CameraParams {\n60:    pub fn lerp(&self, o: &CameraParams, t: f32) -> CameraParams {\n93:    pub fn new(params: CameraParams) -> Self {\n98:    pub fn current(&self) -> CameraParams {\n109:    pub fn blend_from_current(&mut self, seconds: f32) {\n114:    pub fn update(&mut self, focus: Vec3, dt: f32) {\n130:    pub fn snap(&mut self, focus: Vec3) {\n136:    pub fn ground_axes(&self) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\n143:    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\n149:    pub fn up(&self) -> Vec3 {\n155:    pub fn look_at(&self) -> Vec3 {\n159:    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\n163:    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\n186:    pub fn screen_ray(&self, px: Vec2, size: Vec2) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\n196:    pub fn ground_point(&self, px: Vec2, size: Vec2, height: f32) -> Option<Vec3> {\n206:    pub fn relative_move(&self, input: Vec2) -> Vec2 {\n212:    pub fn view_proj(&self, aspect: f32) -> Mat4 {\n    /// table.\n    pub fn materials(&mut self) -> MutexGuard<'_, MaterialTable> {\n        lock(&self.materials)\n    }\n\n    /// Turns simulation events into visual effects (explosions, dust).\n    pub fn add_events(&mut self, events: &[SimEvent]) {\n        for e in events {\n            crate::fx::event_bursts(e, &mut self.pending_particles);\n            if let SimEvent::Explosion { pos, radius } = e {\n                self.shocks.push((*pos, radius * 3.5, self.last_time.unwrap_or(0.0)));\n                self.water_dents.push((*pos, radius * 1.2, 0.22));\n            }\n            if let SimEvent::Splash { pos } = e {\n                self.water_dents.push((*pos, 0.7, 0.12));\n            }\n            if let SimEvent::Destroyed { pos, size } = e {\n                self.shocks.push((*pos, size.max(0.5) * 5.0, self.last_time.unwrap_or(0.0)));\n            }\n            match e {\n                SimEvent::Slam { pos, radius } => self.shocks.push((*pos, radius * 2.5, self.last_time.unwrap_or(0.0))),\n                SimEvent::Blast { pos, .. } => self.shocks.push((*pos, 4.0, self.last_time.unwrap_or(0.0))),\n                _ => {}\n            }\n            match e {\n                SimEvent::Explosion { pos, radius } => {\n                    self.effects.push(Effect { kind: EffectKind::Explosion { radius: *radius }, pos: *pos, start: self.now })\n                }\n                SimEvent::Land { pos, speed } if *speed > 6.0 => {\n                    self.effects.push(Effect { kind: EffectKind::Dust, pos: *pos, start: self.now })\n                }\n                SimEvent::Hit { pos, .. } => self.effects.push(Effect {\n                    kind: EffectKind::Burst { color: [1.0, 0.35, 0.2], up: 0.5 },\n                    pos: *pos,\n                    start: self.now,\n                }),\n                SimEvent::Splash { pos } => self.effects.push(Effect {\n                    kind: EffectKind::Burst { color: [0.75, 0.88, 1.0], up: 2.5 },\n                    pos: *pos + Vec3::Y * 0.3,\n                    start: self.now,\n                }),\n                SimEvent::Break { pos } => self.effects.push(Effect {\n                    kind: EffectKind::Burst { color: [0.85, 0.82, 0.75], up: 1.0 },\n                    pos: *pos,\n                    start: self.now,\n                }),\n                SimEvent::Bounce { pos } => self.effects.push(Effect {\n                    kind: EffectKind::Burst { color: [1.0, 0.6, 0.75], up: 0.5 },\n                    pos: *pos + Vec3::Y * 0.1,\n                    start: self.now,\n                }),\n                SimEvent::Respawn { pos } => self.effects.push(Effect {\n                    kind: EffectKind::Burst { color: [1.0, 1.0, 1.0], up: 1.5 },\n                    pos: *pos + Vec3::Y * 0.4,\n                    start: self.now,\n                }),\n                _ => {}\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn emit_effects(&mut self, scene: &mut Scene) {\n        let now = self.now;\n        self.effects.retain(|e| now - e.start < 1.0);\n        for e in &self.effects {\n            let t = (now - e.start) as f32;\n            match e.kind {\n                EffectKind::Explosion { radius } => {\n                    if t < 0.35 {\n                        let grow = (t / 0.08).min(1.0);\n                        let fade = 1.0 - ((t - 0.08) / 0.27).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\n                        let r = radius * 0.85 * grow * fade.sqrt();\n                        if r > 0.01 {\n                            let mut s = SdfInstance::sphere(e.pos, r, Vec3::new(1.0, 0.62, 0.2));\n                            s.style = Style::Unlit;\n                            s.emissive = 2.0 * fade;\n                            s.flags = rs::flags::NO_SHADOW | rs::flags::NO_CUT;\n                            s.group = 0xfff0;\n                            scene.sdfs.push(s);\n                        }\n                        scene.point_lights.push(rs::PointLight {\n                            position: e.pos + Vec3::Y * 0.5,\n                            color: Vec3::new(1.0, 0.6, 0.25) * 6.0 * fade,\n                            radius: radius * 5.0,\n                            shadows: false,\n                        });\n//! Window events -> egui input. Natively this is egui-winit; in the browser (where egui-winit\n//! does not build) a small adapter covers what the panels use: pointer, wheel, keys and text.\n\nuse winit::event::WindowEvent;\nuse winit::window::Window;\n\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))]\npub struct UiInput(egui_winit::State);\n\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))]\nimpl UiInput {\n    pub fn new(ctx: &egui::Context, window: &Window, max_texture: usize) -> Self {\n        Self(egui_winit::State::new(\n            ctx.clone(),\n            egui::ViewportId::ROOT,\n            window,\n            Some(window.scale_factor() as f32),\n            None,\n            Some(max_texture),\n        ))\n    }\n\n    /// Feeds an event to egui; true when egui used it (the game should ignore it).\n    pub fn on_window_event(&mut self, window: &Window, event: &WindowEvent) -> bool {\n        self.0.on_window_event(window, event).consumed\n    }\n\n    pub fn take(&mut self, window: &Window) -> egui::RawInput {\n        self.0.take_egui_input(window)\n    }\n\n    pub fn platform_output(&mut self, window: &Window, out: egui::PlatformOutput) {\n        self.0.handle_platform_output(window, out);\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]\npub struct UiInput {\n    ctx: egui::Context,\n    raw: egui::RawInput,\nPACK.json\naltar.json\nanvil.json\naxe.json\nbanner.json\nbarrel.json\nbasket.json\nbench.json\nbone_pile.json\nbrazier.json\nbucket.json\ncage.json\ncampfire.json\ncandle_cluster.json\ncanopy_stall.json\ncask.json\nchains.json\nchair.json\nchest.json\ncolumn.json\ncolumn_broken.json\ncooking_pot.json\ncot.json\ncrate_stack.json\ncrystal_cluster.json\nfence.json\ngable_stall.json\ngate.json\nhafted_tool.json\nhall_table.json\n62\n{\"format\":2,\"name\":\"rowboat\",\"unit\":\"cm\",\n\"description\":\"A wooden rowboat on the ground: round hull, pointed bow, stern deck, two thwarts, two oars. Knobs: length, hull, pose.\",\n\"tags\":[\"boat\",\"rowboat\",\"canoe\",\"dinghy\",\"skiff\",\"vehicle\"],\n\"category\":\"town\",\n\"materials\":{\n\"dark\":{\"color\":\"#4f3622\"},\n\"floor\":{\"base\":\"MAT/oak_planks\",\"color\":\"#9a7048\"},\n\"hull\":{\"base\":\"MAT/oak_planks\",\"color\":\"#7a5232\"},\n\"oarwood\":{\"color\":\"#c9a26b\"}},\n\"parts\":{\n\"boat\":{\"pos\":[0,62,0],\"roll\":0,\"parts\":{\n  \"bow\":{\"type\":\"cylinder\",\"radius\":62,\"radius_end\":0,\"height\":80,\"arc\":180,\"facing\":\"-y\",\"pos\":[0,0,110],\"axis\":\"z\",\"mat\":\"hull\"},\n  \"floor\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[50,2,100],\"pos\":[0,-51,-10],\"mat\":\"floor\"},\n  \"mid\":{\"type\":\"tube\",\"radius\":62,\"thickness\":5,\"height\":160,\"arc\":180,\"facing\":\"-y\",\"pos\":[0,0,-10],\"axis\":\"z\",\"mat\":\"hull\"},\n  \"oar\":{\"pos\":[63,2.5,-15],\"yaw\":-70,\"pitch\":-19.5,\"mat\":\"oarwood\",\"mirror\":\"x\",\"parts\":{\n    \"blade\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[15,2.5,52],\"pos\":[0,0,-160]},\n    \"shaft\":{\"type\":\"cylinder\",\"radius\":2.5,\"segments\":6,\"from\":[0,0,40],\"to\":[0,0,-135]}}},\n  \"stern\":{\"type\":\"cylinder\",\"radius\":46,\"radius_end\":62,\"height\":60,\"arc\":180,\"facing\":\"-y\",\"pos\":[0,0,-120],\"axis\":\"z\",\"mat\":\"hull\"},\n  \"thwart\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[118,4,24],\"pos\":[0,-3.5,-10],\"mat\":\"dark\",\"array\":{\"count\":2,\"step\":[0,0,70]}}}}},\n\"params\":{\n\"hull\":{\"choices\":[\"rowboat\",\"canoe\"],\"set\":{\"boat.bow.radius\":[62,40],\"boat.floor.pos.1\":[-51,-29],\"boat.floor.size.0\":[50,40],\"boat.mid.radius\":[62,40],\"boat.pos.1\":[62,40],\"boat.stern.radius\":[46,0.5],\"boat.stern.radius_end\":[62,40],\"boat.thwart.size.0\":[118,74]}},\n\"length\":{\"range\":[200,420],\"set\":{\"boat.bow.height\":0.2667,\"boat.bow.pos.2\":0.3667,\"boat.mid.height\":0.5333,\"boat.mid.pos.2\":-0.0333,\"boat.stern.height\":0.2,\"boat.stern.pos.2\":-0.4,\"boat.thwart.array.step.2\":0.2333,\"boat.thwart.pos.2\":-0.0333}},\n\"pose\":{\"choices\":[\"rowing\",\"beached\",\"bare\"],\"set\":{\"boat.oar.chance\":[1,1,0],\"boat.oar.pitch\":[-19.5,0,0],\"boat.oar.pos.0\":[63,35,35],\"boat.oar.pos.1\":[2.5,1,1],\"boat.oar.pos.2\":[-15,35,35],\"boat.oar.yaw\":[-70,0,0],\"boat.roll\":[0,10,0]}}},\n\"presets\":{\n\"beached\":{\"pose\":\"beached\"},\n\"canoe\":{\"hull\":\"canoe\",\"length\":420,\"pose\":\"bare\"}}}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"a9d4f0e8-9c56-43b6-927c-69f204f48430","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:42:10.435Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# The store's catalogue (rooms/catalogue.toml; body = \"none\"): a pad's signal lays out the next\n# page of the store's object rows (embedded, then the committed packs on disk, then the shipped\n# packs the disk lacks), each beside a 1.8 m figure with its row; `back` pages back; toward = -1\n# grows the page toward -z with its first line at the object (put it by the pads):\n#   behavior = { type = \"catalogue\", signal = \"next\", back = \"back\", per_page = 20, columns = 5 }\n# The clip browser (rooms/clip_browser.toml; body = \"none\"): every [[npc]] whose name starts with\n# `cast` plays the same clip; pads step through the library, jump to a set's first clip or toggle\n# auto-play, and the clip's card lies on the floor at the object:\n#   behavior = { type = \"clip_browser\", next = \"clip_next\", back = \"clip_back\", auto = \"clip_auto\",\n#                cast = \"cast\", hold = 5, start = \"QUATERNIUS/Idle_Loop\",\n#                sets = [[\"clip_set_cmu\", \"CMU\"], [\"clip_set_quaternius\", \"QUATERNIUS\"]] }\n# An imported figure (a shipped pack's, e.g. LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight) can wear any biped\n# [[npc]]: look = { figure = \"LIB/kaykit_adventurers/knight\" }.\n# More object fields: pitch = 20, roll = 0 (tilt in degrees, e.g. ramps), density = 1 (kg/m³:\n# 1 is very light; 50-100 = pushable crates; 400 = wood; 2000 = stone), friction = 0.5,\n# restitution = 0.0 (bounciness 0..1; rapier averages it with the surface underneath),\n# damping = 0 (air drag). Pushing shares momentum: a 70 kg character barely moves 300 kg.\n# Reusable props made in the Object Studio replace shape and colour:\n#   asset = \"BUILTIN/bench\", scale = 1, body = \"fixed\" (or \"none\": no collision),\n#   seed = 3 (a variant: chance, jitter and pick; 0 as authored),\n#   roles = { \"$wall\" = \"#5a6b7c\" } (colours for the theme roles its parts name),\n#   patch = [{ op = \"scale\", by = 0.5 }] (asset_edit patch ops on this copy only: a one-off\n#   variant, such as a defect on show in rooms/limits.toml; publish variants rooms reuse).\n#   `room_check` names any asset the library does not have, or a patch that does not apply.\n# Visual-only effects on any object (never affect the simulation; body = \"none\" for invisible\n# emitters with a tiny sphere shape):\n#   light = { color = \"#ffb060\", radius = 7, intensity = 2.5, flicker = 0.8, pulse = 0,\n#             shadows = true, offset = [0, 0.7, 0] }   (the 4 shadow-casting lights nearest you)\n#   particles = { preset = \"fire\", rate = 0, color = \"\", size = 1, speed = 1, life = 1,\n#                 area = [0, 0, 0], offset = [0, 0.5, 0] }\n#     presets: fire smoke sparks embers fountain snow rain fireflies magic steam dust bubbles\n#     confetti (rate 0 = the preset's; area = spawn box half-size; snow/rain: put it up high and\n#     set ground = -height so drops land on the floor)\n#   distortion = { kind = \"haze\", radius = 1.5, strength = 0.4, period = 1.5, offset = [0, 1, 0] }\n#     (strength 0.3-0.6 reads at the default camera; 1+ melts the picture)\n#     kinds: haze (heat shimmer) | lens (magnify; negative strength shrinks) | ripple | ring\n#     (a shockwave every `period` s). Bombs make shockwaves, sparks and smoke by themselves.\n#   emissive = 2..8 makes an object glow (bloom) and light its surroundings.\n#   sway = \"leaves\" moves it in the wind (canopies, banners; drawing only), \"grass\" draws a tuft.\n# Drivable vehicles (E to get in / out; jump = handbrake / climb, crouch = brake / descend):\n#   vehicle = { kind = \"car\" }   or   vehicle = { kind = \"helicopter\" }\n#   optional: color, accent, size = [half x, y, z], mass, power, max_speed, grip, drift_grip\n#   (rear grip with the handbrake: low = big drifts), steer (deg), climb (helicopter m/s),\n#   ceiling (helicopter: highest flying height above its pad, m; default 14).\n#   `pos` is where it stands; shape/body come from the vehicle. Courses and checkpoints work\n#   while driving (you respawn in the vehicle).\n# Shootable things (bullet hell, targets): the player shoots with the blaster\n# ([params] \"bombs.weapon\" = \"blaster\", \"bombs.fire_interval\" = 0.1, \"bombs.shoot_angle\" = 180\n# for always-north in this file's map (it turns with the room), -1 = at the cursor;\n# \"bombs.shot_range\" = 35 m; \"movement.hitbox\" = 0.12 for a tiny hitbox). Shots fly about\n# 1.1 m above the floor and hit what they touch in 3D, so put targets near that height:\n#   health = { hp = 40, score = 100, signal = \"boss_dead\", finish = true, bar = true,\n#              sway = [3, 5], phases = [{ below = 0.5, behavior = { type = \"emitter\", ... } }] }\n#   (finish: destroying it finishes the running course; bar: boss health bar; sway: drift\n#   amplitude (m) / period (s) along the object's X; phases: new behaviour below a health\n#   fraction). Score adds to the running course and shows in the HUD. A `finish` boss can\n#   stand in for the course's FINISH tile.\n# Soft (deformable) objects ignore `shape`:\n#   soft = { shape = { type = \"cuboid\", half = [0.6, 0.6, 0.6], res = [4, 4, 4] }, stiffness = 6 }\n#   soft = { shape = { type = \"sphere\", radius = 0.6, subdivisions = 2 }, stiffness = 10 }\n#   soft = { shape = { type = \"cloth\", size = [2, 1.5], res = [10, 8], vertical = true },\n#            pin = \"top\", stiffness = 20 }          (vertical = hangs down from pos, else flat +Z)\n#   soft = { shape = { type = \"rope\", to = [0, -3, 0], segments = 16, radius = 0.05 },\n#            pin = \"start\", attach = \"ball\" }        (rope end tied to the object named \"ball\")\n#   also: damping = 0.3, mass = 4 (kg), tear = 0.6 (breaks when stretched 60%),\n#         pin = \"\" | \"top\" | \"start\" | \"end\" | \"ends\" | \"corners\" | \"top_corners\" | \"edge\"\n\n# Joints between named objects (b = \"\" fixes `a` to the world); `at` = anchor, layout space:\n# [[joint]]\n# a = \"door\"\n# b = \"\"\n# at = [3.0, 1.0, 2.0]\n# joint = { type = \"hinge\", axis = [0, 1, 0], limits = [-90, 90] }\n#   joint types: fixed | ball | hinge (axis, limits deg, motor_speed deg/s, motor_force, or\n#   spring + damping to swing back: self-closing doors) | slider (axis, limits m, spring, damping)\n#   | rope (length) | spring (length, stiffness, damping)\n#   Joints to the world measure the object: a vertical slider's limits = [-1, 0.25] travel 1 m\n#   down and 0.25 m up. at_b = [x, y, z] puts b's (or the world's) anchor elsewhere, e.g. a\n#   spring that starts stretched. Keep chain/joint parts a few cm clear of fixed colliders.\n\n# Generated chains and rope bridges (layout space; density defaults to 400):\n# [[chain]]\n# from = [3.0, 4.0, 2.0]\n# to = [3.0, 1.0, 2.0]\n# links = 8\n# radius = 0.07\n# attach_to = \"ball\"          # tie the end to an object (fix_to = true pins it to the world)\n# [[chain]]\n# style = \"bridge\"            # planks hinged edge to edge, both ends fixed\n# from = [2.0, 0.0, 8.5]\n# to = [14.0, 0.0, 8.5]\n# links = 12\n# width = 1.4\n# sag = 0.04                  # hangs 4% of the span lower in the middle\n# damping = 0.3               # air drag on the links (default 0.3); fewer, longer planks are calmer\n\n# Characters and creatures (layout space). kind = biped | spider | lizard | beetle | blob;\n# ai = idle | wander (radius, pause = [min, max]) | patrol (points = [[x, z], ...], pause) |\n10:pub struct CameraParams {\n11-    /// Degrees above the horizon: 90 = straight down, 0 = side view.\n12-    pub tilt: f32,\n13-    /// Degrees; 0 = looking north (-Z).\n14-    pub yaw: f32,\n15-    /// Distance from the focus point (metres). In orthographic mode it sets the zoom.\n16-    pub distance: f32,\n17-    /// Vertical field of view (degrees). Orthographic uses it to match framing.\n18-    pub fov: f32,\n19-    pub ortho: bool,\n20-    /// Seconds for the camera to catch up with the focus (0 = locked).\n21-    pub follow_lag: f32,\n22-    /// Look slightly above the focus point (metres).\n23-    pub height_offset: f32,\n24-}\n25-\n26-impl Default for CameraParams {\n27-    fn default() -> Self {\n28-        Self { tilt: 62.0, yaw: 0.0, distance: 18.0, fov: 40.0, ortho: false, follow_lag: 0.12, height_offset: 0.8 }\n29-    }\n30-}\n31-\n32-impl Tunable for CameraParams {\n60:    pub fn lerp(&self, o: &CameraParams, t: f32) -> CameraParams {\n93:    pub fn new(params: CameraParams) -> Self {\n98:    pub fn current(&self) -> CameraParams {\n109:    pub fn blend_from_current(&mut self, seconds: f32) {\n114:    pub fn update(&mut self, focus: Vec3, dt: f32) {\n130:    pub fn snap(&mut self, focus: Vec3) {\n136:    pub fn ground_axes(&self) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\n143:    pub fn forward(&self) -> Vec3 {\n149:    pub fn up(&self) -> Vec3 {\n155:    pub fn look_at(&self) -> Vec3 {\n159:    pub fn eye(&self) -> Vec3 {\n163:    pub fn data(&self, aspect: f32) -> CameraData {\n186:    pub fn screen_ray(&self, px: Vec2, size: Vec2) -> (Vec3, Vec3) {\n196:    pub fn ground_point(&self, px: Vec2, size: Vec2, height: f32) -> Option<Vec3> {\n206:    pub fn relative_move(&self, input: Vec2) -> Vec2 {\n212:    pub fn view_proj(&self, aspect: f32) -> Mat4 {\n    /// table.\n    pub fn materials(&mut self) -> MutexGuard<'_, MaterialTable> {\n        lock(&self.materials)\n    }\n\n    /// Turns simulation events into visual effects (explosions, dust).\n    pub fn add_events(&mut self, events: &[SimEvent]) {\n        for e in events {\n            crate::fx::event_bursts(e, &mut self.pending_particles);\n            if let SimEvent::Explosion { pos, radius } = e {\n                self.shocks.push((*pos, radius * 3.5, self.last_time.unwrap_or(0.0)));\n                self.water_dents.push((*pos, radius * 1.2, 0.22));\n            }\n            if let SimEvent::Splash { pos } = e {\n                self.water_dents.push((*pos, 0.7, 0.12));\n            }\n            if let SimEvent::Destroyed { pos, size } = e {\n                self.shocks.push((*pos, size.max(0.5) * 5.0, self.last_time.unwrap_or(0.0)));\n            }\n            match e {\n                SimEvent::Slam { pos, radius } => self.shocks.push((*pos, radius * 2.5, self.last_time.unwrap_or(0.0))),\n                SimEvent::Blast { pos, .. } => self.shocks.push((*pos, 4.0, self.last_time.unwrap_or(0.0))),\n                _ => {}\n            }\n            match e {\n                SimEvent::Explosion { pos, radius } => {\n                    self.effects.push(Effect { kind: EffectKind::Explosion { radius: *radius }, pos: *pos, start: self.now })\n                }\n                SimEvent::Land { pos, speed } if *speed > 6.0 => {\n                    self.effects.push(Effect { kind: EffectKind::Dust, pos: *pos, start: self.now })\n                }\n                SimEvent::Hit { pos, .. } => self.effects.push(Effect {\n                    kind: EffectKind::Burst { color: [1.0, 0.35, 0.2], up: 0.5 },\n                    pos: *pos,\n                    start: self.now,\n                }),\n                SimEvent::Splash { pos } => self.effects.push(Effect {\n                    kind: EffectKind::Burst { color: [0.75, 0.88, 1.0], up: 2.5 },\n                    pos: *pos + Vec3::Y * 0.3,\n                    start: self.now,\n                }),\n                SimEvent::Break { pos } => self.effects.push(Effect {\n                    kind: EffectKind::Burst { color: [0.85, 0.82, 0.75], up: 1.0 },\n                    pos: *pos,\n                    start: self.now,\n                }),\n                SimEvent::Bounce { pos } => self.effects.push(Effect {\n                    kind: EffectKind::Burst { color: [1.0, 0.6, 0.75], up: 0.5 },\n                    pos: *pos + Vec3::Y * 0.1,\n                    start: self.now,\n                }),\n                SimEvent::Respawn { pos } => self.effects.push(Effect {\n                    kind: EffectKind::Burst { color: [1.0, 1.0, 1.0], up: 1.5 },\n                    pos: *pos + Vec3::Y * 0.4,\n                    start: self.now,\n                }),\n                _ => {}\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    fn emit_effects(&mut self, scene: &mut Scene) {\n        let now = self.now;\n        self.effects.retain(|e| now - e.start < 1.0);\n        for e in &self.effects {\n            let t = (now - e.start) as f32;\n            match e.kind {\n                EffectKind::Explosion { radius } => {\n                    if t < 0.35 {\n                        let grow = (t / 0.08).min(1.0);\n                        let fade = 1.0 - ((t - 0.08) / 0.27).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\n                        let r = radius * 0.85 * grow * fade.sqrt();\n                        if r > 0.01 {\n                            let mut s = SdfInstance::sphere(e.pos, r, Vec3::new(1.0, 0.62, 0.2));\n                            s.style = Style::Unlit;\n                            s.emissive = 2.0 * fade;\n                            s.flags = rs::flags::NO_SHADOW | rs::flags::NO_CUT;\n                            s.group = 0xfff0;\n                            scene.sdfs.push(s);\n                        }\n                        scene.point_lights.push(rs::PointLight {\n                            position: e.pos + Vec3::Y * 0.5,\n                            color: Vec3::new(1.0, 0.6, 0.25) * 6.0 * fade,\n                            radius: radius * 5.0,\n                            shadows: false,\n                        });\n//! Window events -> egui input. Natively this is egui-winit; in the browser (where egui-winit\n//! does not build) a small adapter covers what the panels use: pointer, wheel, keys and text.\n\nuse winit::event::WindowEvent;\nuse winit::window::Window;\n\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))]\npub struct UiInput(egui_winit::State);\n\n#[cfg(not(target_arch = \"wasm32\"))]\nimpl UiInput {\n    pub fn new(ctx: &egui::Context, window: &Window, max_texture: usize) -> Self {\n        Self(egui_winit::State::new(\n            ctx.clone(),\n            egui::ViewportId::ROOT,\n            window,\n            Some(window.scale_factor() as f32),\n            None,\n            Some(max_texture),\n        ))\n    }\n\n    /// Feeds an event to egui; true when egui used it (the game should ignore it).\n    pub fn on_window_event(&mut self, window: &Window, event: &WindowEvent) -> bool {\n        self.0.on_window_event(window, event).consumed\n    }\n\n    pub fn take(&mut self, window: &Window) -> egui::RawInput {\n        self.0.take_egui_input(window)\n    }\n\n    pub fn platform_output(&mut self, window: &Window, out: egui::PlatformOutput) {\n        self.0.handle_platform_output(window, out);\n    }\n}\n\n#[cfg(target_arch = \"wasm32\")]\npub struct UiInput {\n    ctx: egui::Context,\n    raw: egui::RawInput,\nPACK.json\naltar.json\nanvil.json\naxe.json\nbanner.json\nbarrel.json\nbasket.json\nbench.json\nbone_pile.json\nbrazier.json\nbucket.json\ncage.json\ncampfire.json\ncandle_cluster.json\ncanopy_stall.json\ncask.json\nchains.json\nchair.json\nchest.json\ncolumn.json\ncolumn_broken.json\ncooking_pot.json\ncot.json\ncrate_stack.json\ncrystal_cluster.json\nfence.json\ngable_stall.json\ngate.json\nhafted_tool.json\nhall_table.json\n62\n{\"format\":2,\"name\":\"rowboat\",\"unit\":\"cm\",\n\"description\":\"A wooden rowboat on the ground: round hull, pointed bow, stern deck, two thwarts, two oars. Knobs: length, hull, pose.\",\n\"tags\":[\"boat\",\"rowboat\",\"canoe\",\"dinghy\",\"skiff\",\"vehicle\"],\n\"category\":\"town\",\n\"materials\":{\n\"dark\":{\"color\":\"#4f3622\"},\n\"floor\":{\"base\":\"MAT/oak_planks\",\"color\":\"#9a7048\"},\n\"hull\":{\"base\":\"MAT/oak_planks\",\"color\":\"#7a5232\"},\n\"oarwood\":{\"color\":\"#c9a26b\"}},\n\"parts\":{\n\"boat\":{\"pos\":[0,62,0],\"roll\":0,\"parts\":{\n  \"bow\":{\"type\":\"cylinder\",\"radius\":62,\"radius_end\":0,\"height\":80,\"arc\":180,\"facing\":\"-y\",\"pos\":[0,0,110],\"axis\":\"z\",\"mat\":\"hull\"},\n  \"floor\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[50,2,100],\"pos\":[0,-51,-10],\"mat\":\"floor\"},\n  \"mid\":{\"type\":\"tube\",\"radius\":62,\"thickness\":5,\"height\":160,\"arc\":180,\"facing\":\"-y\",\"pos\":[0,0,-10],\"axis\":\"z\",\"mat\":\"hull\"},\n  \"oar\":{\"pos\":[63,2.5,-15],\"yaw\":-70,\"pitch\":-19.5,\"mat\":\"oarwood\",\"mirror\":\"x\",\"parts\":{\n    \"blade\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[15,2.5,52],\"pos\":[0,0,-160]},\n    \"shaft\":{\"type\":\"cylinder\",\"radius\":2.5,\"segments\":6,\"from\":[0,0,40],\"to\":[0,0,-135]}}},\n  \"stern\":{\"type\":\"cylinder\",\"radius\":46,\"radius_end\":62,\"height\":60,\"arc\":180,\"facing\":\"-y\",\"pos\":[0,0,-120],\"axis\":\"z\",\"mat\":\"hull\"},\n  \"thwart\":{\"type\":\"box\",\"size\":[118,4,24],\"pos\":[0,-3.5,-10],\"mat\":\"dark\",\"array\":{\"count\":2,\"step\":[0,0,70]}}}}},\n\"params\":{\n\"hull\":{\"choices\":[\"rowboat\",\"canoe\"],\"set\":{\"boat.bow.radius\":[62,40],\"boat.floor.pos.1\":[-51,-29],\"boat.floor.size.0\":[50,40],\"boat.mid.radius\":[62,40],\"boat.pos.1\":[62,40],\"boat.stern.radius\":[46,0.5],\"boat.stern.radius_end\":[62,40],\"boat.thwart.size.0\":[118,74]}},\n\"length\":{\"range\":[200,420],\"set\":{\"boat.bow.height\":0.2667,\"boat.bow.pos.2\":0.3667,\"boat.mid.height\":0.5333,\"boat.mid.pos.2\":-0.0333,\"boat.stern.height\":0.2,\"boat.stern.pos.2\":-0.4,\"boat.thwart.array.step.2\":0.2333,\"boat.thwart.pos.2\":-0.0333}},\n\"pose\":{\"choices\":[\"rowing\",\"beached\",\"bare\"],\"set\":{\"boat.oar.chance\":[1,1,0],\"boat.oar.pitch\":[-19.5,0,0],\"boat.oar.pos.0\":[63,35,35],\"boat.oar.pos.1\":[2.5,1,1],\"boat.oar.pos.2\":[-15,35,35],\"boat.oar.yaw\":[-70,0,0],\"boat.roll\":[0,10,0]}}},\n\"presets\":{\n\"beached\":{\"pose\":\"beached\"},\n\"canoe\":{\"hull\":\"canoe\",\"length\":420,\"pose\":\"bare\"}}}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Vwg86QVs3fM4fRVoDsyXtf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
