{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012EKVg9geKJxxbnNctKfMvh","type":"tool_result","content":"314:## Test it\n315-\n316-The harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\n317-and runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\n318-to the game:\n319-\n320-```bash\n321-curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n322-curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\n323-curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\n324-python3 -m http.server 8000\n325-```\n326-\n327-Then open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\n328-The hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n329-`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n330-`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n331-`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n332-\n333-The checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n334-`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n335-`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n336-\n337-- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n338-- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n339-- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n340-  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n341-- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n342-  player of its own;\n343-- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n344-  told the round ended;\n345-- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n346-\n347-**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\n348-cases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n349-`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\n350-game is served from the harness's own origin.\n351-\n352-In the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\n353-checks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\n354-runs there.\nFAIL the pad moves the focus: 0 -> 0\nFAIL prompts show PlayStation glyphs on a pad: ['W S:Choose', 'Space:Confirm']\nFAIL the device is the pad: keys\nFAIL the pad confirms: title\nFAIL keys move the focus: 0\nFAIL Esc backs: slots\nFAIL mouse hover moves the focus: 0\nFAIL a click activates: slots\nFAIL Settings lists glyphs: ['Guest 1', 'Guest 2', 'Guest 3', 'Guest 4']\nFAIL Xbox glyphs after the option: ['Mouse Right:Back']\nFAIL back to the title: names\nFAIL attract starts about 10 s after the last input: 25.0 s, title\nFAIL Pixel 7: a tap opens Settings: attract\nFAIL Galaxy Tab S4: a tap opens Settings: attract\n30 passed, 14 failed","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"f18908a7-2a26-4bd0-b8be-75e3260179e2","timestamp":"2026-11-05T06:42:59.309Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"314:## Test it\n315-\n316-The harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\n317-and runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\n318-to the game:\n319-\n320-```bash\n321-curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n322-curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\n323-curl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\n324-python3 -m http.server 8000\n325-```\n326-\n327-Then open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\n328-The hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n329-`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n330-`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n331-`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n332-\n333-The checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n334-`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n335-`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n336-\n337-- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n338-- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n339-- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n340-  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n341-- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n342-  player of its own;\n343-- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n344-  told the round ended;\n345-- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n346-\n347-**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\n348-cases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n349-`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\n350-game is served from the harness's own origin.\n351-\n352-In the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\n353-checks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\n354-runs there.\nFAIL the pad moves the focus: 0 -> 0\nFAIL prompts show PlayStation glyphs on a pad: ['W S:Choose', 'Space:Confirm']\nFAIL the device is the pad: keys\nFAIL the pad confirms: title\nFAIL keys move the focus: 0\nFAIL Esc backs: slots\nFAIL mouse hover moves the focus: 0\nFAIL a click activates: slots\nFAIL Settings lists glyphs: ['Guest 1', 'Guest 2', 'Guest 3', 'Guest 4']\nFAIL Xbox glyphs after the option: ['Mouse Right:Back']\nFAIL back to the title: names\nFAIL attract starts about 10 s after the last input: 25.0 s, title\nFAIL Pixel 7: a tap opens Settings: attract\nFAIL Galaxy Tab S4: a tap opens Settings: attract\n30 passed, 14 failed","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012EKVg9geKJxxbnNctKfMvh","permi