{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjQSSsNmTTGU8f2xDEbq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DXRyHEiPVHmPVa2rFRTmoG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef patch(path, pairs):\n    s = open(path).read()\n    for a, b in pairs:\n        assert a in s, (path, a[:80])\n        s = s.replace(a, b, 1)\n    open(path, 'w').write(s)\npatch('crates/pav_core/tests/fit.rs',[\n(\"\"\"    press(&mut sim, b::BACK);\n    assert_eq!(screen(&sim), \"attract\");\n    // Behind the card\"\"\",\"\"\"    // A finger has no Back button, so Settings has one it can tap.\n    let m = game(&sim).menu().unwrap();\n    let back = m.items.iter().position(|i| i.act == pav_core::games::fit::menus::MAct::Close).unwrap();\n    sim.step(&InputFrame { ui: Some(UiEvent::Click(back as u16)), ..Default::default() });\n    assert_eq!(screen(&sim), \"attract\");\n    // Behind the card\"\"\"),\n])\npatch('crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/screens.rs',[\n(\"\"\"                let items = vec![\n                    MItem::slider(MAct::Music, \"Music\", s.music, pct(s.music)),\"\"\",\"\"\"                let mut items = vec![\n                    MItem::slider(MAct::Music, \"Music\", s.music, pct(s.music)),\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"                    MItem::button(MAct::ResetSave, \"Reset Save\"),\n                ];\n                base(\"settings\", \"Settings\", items)\"\"\",\"\"\"                    MItem::button(MAct::ResetSave, \"Reset Save\"),\n                ];\n                if self.boot.touch_only {\n                    // A finger has no Back button.\n                    items.insert(0, MItem::button(MAct::Close, \"Back\"));\n                }\n                base(\"settings\", \"Settings\", items)\"\"\"),\n])\nEOF\ncat > ../README.md <<'EOF'\n# Whiff Fit: how this folder works\n\nA five-day balance comedy at a resort staffed by talking gym equipment, built on the Pavilion\nengine (Shardfall). `PLAN.md` in the parent folder is the design this was built from.\n\n## Layout\n- `engine/`: the engine, with the game in `crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/`:\n  - `mod.rs` the `FitGame` state, `flow.rs` what each screen does in a tick, `screens.rs` every menu\n    and screen as data, `run.rs` card/3-2-1/play/result, `events/*.rs` one file per event,\n    `check.rs` the morning test, `finale.rs` the Big Stand, `medley.rs` the Medley,\n    `meta.rs` saves and wardrobe, `bot.rs` the bot that plays it all.\n  - Data: `rules.toml` (every number), `script.toml` (all the words), `charts.toml` (Step Party),\n    `sets/*.toml` (one room per set).\n  - `crates/pav_ui/src/fit_ui.rs` draws the UI the sim describes; `crates/pav_audio/src/music.rs` and\n    `voice.rs` are the songs and gibberish; `crates/pav_app/src/weblink.rs` joins the game and its page.\n- `tools/`: `make_props.py`, `make_sets.py`, `make_clips.py` write the JSON props, TOML sets and\n  `anim/fit.json`; `build.sh` builds the one-file page; `tour.py`, `shots.sh` take captures.\n- `tests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]`: the one test command. Prints failures and a count.\n- `hub/`: the AI Hub client and harness, as downloaded.\n- `notes/`: decisions, testing feedback, credits.\n\nRunning from `engine/`, `pav` reads `rules.toml`, `script.toml`, `charts.toml` and the sets from\ndisk at every `load`, so changing them needs no rebuild: `./target/debug/pav play scene=fit bot=true`.\nThe browser build embeds them. Add `?fast=1` to the page to skip shadows and ripples on software renderers.\n\n## Add an event\n1. Copy `events/breath.rs`; give it `start`, `tick` (returns `Some(score)` at the end), `stop`, `hud`, `bot`.\n2. Add a line each to `EventKind` (key, name, coach, opening day, set, lane), `ALL`, `EventState` and its `each!` macro, in `events/mod.rs`.\n3. Add it to a pavilion in `island.rs`, `card.<key>` lines in `script.toml`, a group in `rules.rs` and `rules.toml`.\n4. `tests/fit.rs` then requires its bot to earn 2 stars and idle input to earn none. Add it to `ATTRACT` in `flow.rs`.\n\n## Add a set\nAdd a function to `tools/make_sets.py` (or write `sets/<name>.toml` by hand: a `stage` marker, `[view]`, objects), add it to `Set` and `SETS` in `world.rs`.\n\n## Add a song\nWrite a function in `pav_audio/src/music.rs` (tracks of a patch and a pattern of scale degrees over a chord progression), add it to `song()`, a constant in `world.rs`'s `song` module, and play it with `SimEvent::Music`.\nEOF\ncat > ../notes/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n# Decisions the plan left open\n- Title: Whiff Fit, one of 50 brainstormed, picked with Python's `secrets`.\n- Sets have no `[camera]`: every camera comes from cues, because a room camera applied in the same frame as a cue overrode it.\n- All game logic runs in `Game::pre`; `post` only filters the character's own Land/Jump/Splash events, since events place figures by hand.\n- One water zone per set (three for the channel), not one per tile: `merge_zones` per tile and grid per zone cost 98% of the frame.\n- Frames show only the current set (`World.only_current`), and rewind history is off in the game (the test turns it on).\n- The Commodore on the island is a prop on a mooring post (with his mark as the talk spot); flying gulls are the three-entity rigs.\n- Judges are gull props on a raft; the score cards are UI, big enough for 10 feet.\n- Tray Trek's glasses keep sliding until tilted back (no spring to the centre), so idle input loses them. Score 180 per glass plus 100 no-spill (plan said 200 plus a bonus, capped at 1000).\n- Breath Bloom's ring only counts while the breath is near the guide; Tempo Squats only credits reps you went down for; otherwise doing nothing earned a star.\n- Morning Lap ends itself at 130 s so an idle player isn't stuck; Paddle Slalom likewise at 110 s.\n- The wardrobe opens only from the island (it needs the camera and the figure); the mat at the pier and the Schedule both start the Big Stand.\n- Sleep needs the day's goal; repeats always bank one minute, so nobody is ever stuck.\n- Settings gains a Back row on touch-only devices, since a finger has no Back button.\n- Tests run with `?fast=1` (no shadows or ripples): on a shared software-rendered machine the page otherwise ran under 2 ticks a second.\nEOF\ncd .. && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\ns=open('../PROGRESS.md').read()\ns=s.replace(\"Remaining: final look at a few screens at 1080p, README.md, notes/decisions.md, notes/feedback.md,\",\"README and decisions written. Remaining: final look at a few screens at 1080p, notes/feedback.md,\")\nopen('../PROGRESS.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\ntools/build.sh 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c150-260; timeout 590 tests/run.sh browser 2>&1 | tail -6 | cut -c1-400","description":"Add tap-usable Back, write README and decisions, rebuild and test","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":710,"cache_read_input_tokens":796714,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":710},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"7c43fedf-2a6d-4d75-8d42-73c89bfc7900","timestamp":"2026-11-05T07:42:40.015Z","request_id":"req_011CgjQSSWJ2VywtuYqstGty","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DXRyHEiPVHmPVa2rFRTmoG":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223859__x35112d/work/WhiffFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-223859/engine && python3 - <<'EOF'\ndef patch(path, pairs):\n    s = open(path).read()\n    for a, b in pairs:\n        assert a in s, (path, a[:80])\n        s = s.replace(a, b, 1)\n    open(path, 'w').write(s)\npatch('crates/pav_core/tests/fit.rs',[\n(\"\"\"    press(&mut sim, b::BACK);\n    assert_eq!(screen(&sim), \"attract\");\n    // Behind the card\"\"\",\"\"\"    // A finger has no Back button, so Settings has one it can tap.\n    let m = game(&sim).menu().unwrap();\n    let back = m.items.iter().position(|i| i.act == pav_core::games::fit::menus::MAct::Close).unwrap();\n    sim.step(&InputFrame { ui: Some(UiEvent::Click(back as u16)), ..Default::default() });\n    assert_eq!(screen(&sim), \"attract\");\n    // Behind the card\"\"\"),\n])\npatch('crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/screens.rs',[\n(\"\"\"                let items = vec![\n                    MItem::slider(MAct::Music, \"Music\", s.music, pct(s.music)),\"\"\",\"\"\"                let mut items = vec![\n                    MItem::slider(MAct::Music, \"Music\", s.music, pct(s.music)),\"\"\"),\n(\"\"\"                    MItem::button(MAct::ResetSave, \"Reset Save\"),\n                ];\n                base(\"settings\", \"Settings\", items)\"\"\",\"\"\"                    MItem::button(MAct::ResetSave, \"Reset Save\"),\n                ];\n                if self.boot.touch_only {\n                    // A finger has no Back button.\n                    items.insert(0, MItem::button(MAct::Close, \"Back\"));\n                }\n                base(\"settings\", \"Settings\", items)\"\"\"),\n])\nEOF\ncat > ../README.md <<'EOF'\n# Whiff Fit: how this folder works\n\nA five-day balance comedy at a resort staffed by talking gym equipment, built on the Pavilion\nengine (Shardfall). `PLAN.md` in the parent folder is the design this was built from.\n\n## Layout\n- `engine/`: the engine, with the game in `crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/`:\n  - `mod.rs` the `FitGame` state, `flow.rs` what each screen does in a tick, `screens.rs` every menu\n    and screen as data, `run.rs` card/3-2-1/play/result, `events/*.rs` one file per event,\n    `check.rs` the morning test, `finale.rs` the Big Stand, `medley.rs` the Medley,\n    `meta.rs` saves and wardrobe, `bot.rs` the bot that plays it all.\n  - Data: `rules.toml` (every number), `script.toml` (all the words), `charts.toml` (Step Party),\n    `sets/*.toml` (one room per set).\n  - `crates/pav_ui/src/fit_ui.rs` draws the UI the sim describes; `crates/pav_audio/src/music.rs` and\n    `voice.rs` are the songs and gibberish; `crates/pav_app/src/weblink.rs` joins the game and its page.\n- `tools/`: `make_props.py`, `make_sets.py`, `make_clips.py` write the JSON props, TOML sets and\n  `anim/fit.json`; `build.sh` builds the one-file page; `tour.py`, `shots.sh` take captures.\n- `tests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]`: the one test command. Prints failures and a count.\n- `hub/`: the AI Hub client and harness, as downloaded.\n- `notes/`: decisions, testing feedback, credits.\n\nRunning from `engine/`, `pav` reads `rules.toml`, `script.toml`, `charts.toml` and the sets from\ndisk at every `load`, so changing them needs no rebuild: `./target/debug/pav play scene=fit bot=true`.\nThe browser build embeds them. Add `?fast=1` to the page to skip shadows and ripples on software renderers.\n\n## Add an event\n1. Copy `events/breath.rs`; give it `start`, `tick` (returns `Some(score)` at the end), `stop`, `hud`, `bot`.\n2. Add a line each to `EventKind` (key, name, coach, opening day, set, lane), `ALL`, `EventState` and its `each!` macro, in `events/mod.rs`.\n3. Add it to a pavilion in `island.rs`, `card.<key>` lines in `script.toml`, a group in `rules.rs` and `rules.toml`.\n4. `tests/fit.rs` then requires its bot to earn 2 stars and idle input to earn none. Add it to `ATTRACT` in `flow.rs`.\n\n## Add a set\nAdd a function to `tools/make_sets.py` (or write `sets/<name>.toml` by hand: a `stage` marker, `[view]`, objects), add it to `Set` and `SETS` in `world.rs`.\n\n## Add a song\nWrite a function in `pav_audio/src/music.rs` (tracks of a patch and a pattern of scale degrees over a chord progression), add it to `song()`, a constant in `world.rs`'s `song` module, and play it with `SimEvent::Music`.\nEOF\ncat > ../notes/decisions.md <<'EOF'\n# Decisions the plan left open\n- Title: Whiff Fit, one of 50 brainstormed, picked with Python's `secrets`.\n- Sets have no `[camera]`: every camera comes from cues, because a room camera applied in the same frame as a cue overrode it.\n- All game logic runs in `Game::pre`; `post` only filters the character's own Land/Jump/Splash events, since events place figures by hand.\n- One water zone per set (three for the channel), not one per tile: `merge_zones` per tile and grid per zone cost 98% of the frame.\n- Frames show only the current set (`World.only_current`), and rewind history is off in the game (the test turns it on).\n- The Commodore on the island is a prop on a mooring post (with his mark as the talk spot); flying gulls are the three-entity rigs.\n- Judges are gull props on a raft; the score cards are UI, big enough for 10 feet.\n- Tray Trek's glasses keep sliding until tilted back (no spring to the centre), so idle input loses them. Score 180 per glass plus 100 no-spill (plan said 200 plus a bonus, capped at 1000).\n- Breath Bloom's ring only counts while the breath is near the guide; Tempo Squats only credits reps you went down for; otherwise doing nothing earned a star.\n- Morning Lap ends itself at 130 s so an idle player isn't stuck; Paddle Slalom likewise at 110 s.\n- The wardrobe opens only from the island (it needs the camera and the figure); the mat at the pier and the Schedule both start the Big Stand.\n- Sleep needs the day's goal; repeats always bank one minute, so nobody is ever stuck.\n- Settings gains a Back row on touch-only devices, since a finger has no Back button.\n- Tests run with `?fast=1` (no shadows or ripples): on a shared software-rendered machine the page otherwise ran under 2 ticks a second.\nEOF\ncd .. && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\ns=open('../PROGRESS.md').read()\ns=s.replace(\"Remaining: final look at a few screens at 1080p, README.md, notes/decisions.md, notes/feedback.md,\",\"README and decisions written. Remaining: final look at a few screens at 1080p, notes/feedback.md,\")\nopen('../PROGRESS.md','w').write(s)\nEOF\ntools/build.sh 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c150-260; timeout 590 tests/run.sh browser 2>&1 | tail -6 | cut -c1-400","description":"Add tap-usable Back, write README and decisions, rebuild and test","timeout":900000}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01DXRyHEiPVHmPVa2rFRTmoG":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223859__x35112d/work/WhiffFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-223859/engine"}}}
