{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<system-reminder>\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Read, ScheduleWakeup, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\n</system-reminder>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - The user ran `/goal` with: \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\" A session-scoped Stop hook enforces this and blocks stopping until the condition holds.\n   - STAGE.md says: \"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\"\n   - TASK.md: original game inspired by Wii Fit; title a playful riff picked by real RNG from 50 brainstormed; single HTML `[GameTitle-SOURCE-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-223859].html` in root; dev subfolder of the same name; built on Shardfall/Pavilion engine; all audio in code, gibberish voices, music 10% default; AI Hub multiplayer; dev mode from pause with live sliders and reset; attract mode after 10 s; controller-first 10-foot UI, PlayStation glyphs with Xbox option, native keyboard and mouse; touch-only shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" plus Settings, attract runs; no TODOs or stubs; Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback in chat reply AND in-game About/Credits; `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML in the exact shape, \"usage\": \"added on import\"; one test command printing only failures and a one-line count.\n   - PLAN.md: 18-section design (\"Tippy Cay\" resort, Pip, Posey, Big Kettle, Bounce, Commodore Gull, Marjorie, Two-Towel Tom, the Twins; Balance Core; 11 events plus Big Stand; Morning Wobble Check and Balance Age; Minute Clam, Calendar, wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You ghosts; Medley; Play Together; hub ghost mode; dev mode; tests; finishing steps).\n   - Constraints to keep obeying (TASK.md, verbatim): \"Do not read files outside what you need: other agents work in the folders beside this one. They share this machine's ports and processes too. Prefer file:// and the engine's headless tools. If you need a server (the AI Hub harness does), bind 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks (`python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` prints it) and confirm the page is your game before trusting a result. Stop only processes you started, by their PID: never pkill, killall, fuser -k, or kill whatever holds a port.\" \"Don't use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\" \"Keep one or two browsers open at once, and close them when you're done.\" \"Keep every file you make inside your own folder, not /tmp or a parent folder: /tmp is shared.\" \"The browsers are already downloaded: don't run `playwright install` or `playwright install-deps`.\" \"Run your own Playwright scripts with plain `python3`.\" System: the user's email is only for identifying the user, never send it to a service. Commit or push only when asked (no commits were made).\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Pavilion engine (Rust 1.98.1): fixed 60-tick deterministic sim, `Game` trait hook, room TOML sets, format-2 JSON props, motion clips, WebGPU via wgpu, egui painter UI, cpal audio, gilrs pads, wasm-bindgen 0.2.129, single-file packer `scripts/pack_single_html.py`.\n   - All game state in the sim: UI is a node list at virtual 1920x1080 (`UiFrame`), menus as data (`Menu`, `MItem`, `MAct`), so pad, keys, mouse, bot and tests share one path.\n   - Frozen ticks (`Game::frozen`), `World.only_current` (draw only current set), one water zone per set, cue-only cameras, history off in game.\n   - Sample-accurate sequencer with buses, formant voices, rhythm clock via `song_pos`.\n   - AI Hub session client 1.4.0, ghost mode, harness `?game=&players=&latency=&jitter=&loss=&scenario=&auto=1`, `window.__hubCheck.pass`.\n   - Playwright with Chromium software WebGPU flags `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`, stub pad, test-only `?fast=1` page switch.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (root `/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223859__x35112d/work`; dev folder `WhiffFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-223859/`):\n   - Hand-ins, all present: `WhiffFit-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-223859.html` (12,396,882 bytes, built 03:41), `exit-interview.json` (03:37), `PROGRESS.md` (status \"Done... Only the final reply remained\").\n   - `engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/`: `mod.rs` (FitGame, Flow, Overlay, Dev, Boot, `build`, `install_boot`, status), `flow.rs` (`drive`, transitions, island, menus, attract, `activate`), `screens.rs` (`menu()`, `build_ui`, HOW_TO), `run.rs` (EventRun), `events/{mod,breath,pose,squats,plank,step,spin,lap,tide,paddle,tray,dive}.rs`, `check.rs`, `finale.rs`, `medley.rs`, `meta.rs`, `menus.rs`, `ui_model.rs`, `core.rs`, `dialog.rs`, `ghost.rs`, `island.rs`, `world.rs`, `bot.rs`, `rules.rs`, `script.rs`; data `rules.toml`, `script.toml`, `charts.toml`, `sets/*.toml` (9 sets).\n   - Engine patches: `pav_core/src/{input,frame,games/mod,sim,puppet,parts,world,course}.rs`; `pav_view/src/{build,fx}.rs`; `pav_tools/src/{tools,session}.rs`; `pav_ui/src/{lib,headless,fit_ui}.rs`, `pav_ui/fonts/` (Fredoka, Nunito, OFL texts); `pav_audio/src/{lib,music,voice}.rs`; `pav_app/src/{app,input,settings,simhost,main,weblink}.rs`; `web/index.html`; `anim/fit.json`; `assets/props/lib/core/*.json`; `crates/pav_core/tests/fit.rs`.\n   - Hub ready fallback in `engine/web/index.html` (deliberate departure from the plan's block, recorded in `notes/decisions.md`):\n     ```js\n     // Ready at the first status. A slow GPU can spend a long time compiling pipelines with the game\n     // already loaded: rather than sit out the round, it says ready and joins at its first frame.\n     const t0 = performance.now();\n     const waitReady = () => ((window.__gameStatus || (performance.now() - t0 > 12000 && document.querySelector('canvas'))) ? AIHub.ready() : setTimeout(waitReady, 50));\n     ```\n   - `script.rs`: `fill` now ends in `singulars(&s)`, which turns \"1 minutes\", \"1 more minutes\", \"1 days\", \"1 real days\", \"1 shells\" singular unless preceded by a digit or '.'.\n   - `tools/`: `build.sh`, `make_props.py`, `make_sets.py`, `make_clips.py`, `make_rules.py`, `tour.py`, `shots.sh`, `menus.sh`, `island.sh`.\n   - `tests/`: `run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]`, `common.py`, `browser.py` (includes the page-alone test: copied alone to `tests/_alone`, `offline=True`, title `Whiff Fit — A balance comedy at Tippy Cay`, no other requests), `hub.py` (prints only failed check names; includes \"the served page is this game\"), `look.py` (1080p screenshots into `engine/out/`), `boot_time.py`.\n   - `notes/`: `decisions.md`, `feedback.md` (26 issues, 4 critical), `credits.txt`, `engine.diff`, `last_test_run.txt` (126 passed, 0 failed). `README.md` (how to add an event, set, song; mentions commit 49ef2ba). `hub/` (client and harness as downloaded).\n   - Removed in cleanup: `engine/target`, `engine/out`, `engine/.git`, `tests/_served`, `tests/_alone`, `tests/__pycache__`, `tests/last_run.txt`. Any further code change needs a full rebuild (about 2-3 min for each target) and there is no git in `engine/`.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Under 2 ticks/s in the browser: per-tile water zones through `merge_zones` plus a grid per rectangle. Fixed with one zone per set (three bands in the channel) and `World.only_current`.\n   - Figures sank through decks, posts, rafts: no colliders (`body=\"fixed\"`, solid parts).\n   - Player left at the Studio after the check, empty sky: `to_island` now places at the desk.\n   - Touch-only attract bot pressed Back on the touch card, closing Settings: attract's bot only plays events, auto only when no overlays; Settings got a tap-usable Back on touch-only.\n   - First pointer delta 0 hid hover; unbound keys weren't \"any input\"; touch release lost pointer position (uses the release event's position).\n   - `pav load` dropped the first camera cue (`cue_serial = u64::MAX` in `reset_camera`).\n   - 8 prop schema errors from `room_check` (sphere arc → lathe, categories, ref fields, point limits 64), `AiDef` needs `{ type = \"idle\" }`, guest `belt` under `gear`.\n   - Compile error in `fit_ui` hover memory (match arms), which also silently left an old page in place once.\n   - Paddle gust too strong; idle earned stars on Breath and Squats; six events saturated at 1000 (tuned via human-ish balance table); click on Pip never arrived (within 2 m now counts); walking off land (on_land margin, sea recovery); Big Stand plank scoring and lines; engine Land/Jump/Splash spam filtered; prompt rows clipped (measured `PromptRow` in fit_ui); calendar and pass cards double-dimmed; Step Party song started at the card (now at first play tick, finale band restarts at its phase).\n   - Harness intermittently failed \"ready without a key press\" with 3-4 copies under load (copies stuck in `scope.pop().await` while pipelines compile; harness limit 20 s, protocol sits out). Fixed with the 12 s fallback above; failure output made readable.\n   - Browser stay test failed at load 56: pad taps ended before a frame saw them; waits now follow ticks up to 40 s.\n   - Native-run finding \"1 minutes for the Clam\" and code-read finding Pip's wave line unfilled `{n}`, \"1 shells\", \"1 days. There were 1\": fixed with `singulars`, `pip.absence1`, `waves` counter, and tests.\n   - ImageMagick `import` has no X11 here: used `ffmpeg -f x11grab`.\n   - `tests/look.py` was stopped by `timeout 380` on the final build after taking the title and About page 1 shots (later pages not captured on this build).\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   Verified on the final page (built 03:41):\n   - `tests/run.sh all`: 126 passed, 0 failed in one run, including bot New Stay to credits on 3 seeds, each event's bot and idle outcomes, browser with pad, keys, mouse, touch profiles, WebKit fallback, sound level, standalone page, harness at 2/3/4 players, bad network, host leaving, solo check, client byte-compare.\n   - Native window under xvfb with a scripted pad through one full event (no panics); an earlier build went from title to look screen.\n   - 1080p title and About page 1 viewed from `file://`. An earlier build's look also confirmed About pages 1, 4 and 7 of 9. No console errors in the earlier full look; the final run's script was terminated before printing errors.\n   - On-disk audit script: \"audit problems: none\" (hand-ins, interview shape, About text equals interview, title, hub tags and client byte for byte, no external refs, 21 FIT clips, 9 library clips, 23 FIT clips played, 27 props placed, 8 library props, 118-char script limit, no TODO/FIXME, notes, tests, cleanup).\n   Not verifiable here (TASK.md: \"No script can check these... anything that needs the real thing is checked as far as it can be here, never required\"): real controller, touch device, TV, a second person, anyone listening or playtesting.\n   Exit interview content for the final reply:\n   - Source Information: Date 2026-11-04 22:38:59; Source Wii Fit; Plan PLAN.md; Genre: Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame (daily ritual, unlocks, wardrobe); Perspective: Third person, a camera per activity: 3/4 follow on the island, mirror-style front view for exercises, chase for the lap, paddle and tray, high 3/4 for the raft, side view for the dives; Tech: Rust 1.98.1 compiled to WebAssembly with WebGPU; Pavilion engine (Shardfall repository, commit 49ef2ba, changed for this game): rapier3d 0.36 physics, wgpu renderer, egui 0.36 painter UI, cpal audio, gilrs gamepads; wasm-bindgen 0.2.129; one self-contained HTML file with no external dependencies; AI Hub session client 1.4.0; Art Direction: engine's cel-shaded rounded primitives with thin ink outlines, taken high-key and pastel: 37 hand-written props, nine sets, a painted UI in Fredoka and Nunito; Animation: engine's procedural puppet with motion clips: 25 hand-keyed clips (FIT set) plus library clips from Mesh2Motion, CMU, 100STYLE and Quaternius; poses scrubbed by gameplay; whole-figure lean about the feet; Audio: all in code with no audio files: six sequenced songs (bossa, pads, waltz, funk-pop, mallets, march), 43 synthesized sound effects and stingers, Animalese-style gibberish voices from formant-filtered blips with a timbre per speaker, music at 10% by default; Online: AI Hub session (ghost mode, 1 to 4 players): the Inter-Resort Medley with other players as seat-coloured ghosts in neighbouring lanes; solo: Play Together passes one pad among 2 to 4 guests, and Yesterday You ghosts of your own best runs; Testing: headless only: Rust tests with a bot that plays New Stay to the credits, each event on five seeds, balance tables with a human-like player; Playwright in Chromium with a stub pad, keys, mouse, phone and tablet profiles and WebKit iPhone; the AI Hub harness at 2 to 4 players on a bad network and with the host leaving; captures for composition; the native window under xvfb, driven by a scripted pad through the menus and one full event; no physical controller, touch device, TV or second person; nobody listened to the sound; Research: none beyond the plan's own short web search on Wii Fit; read the engine's docs and source and the AI Hub protocol; Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; Model: Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh; Usage: added on import.\n   - Testing Feedback: 26 issues, counted in notes/feedback.md as I went. | 4: the page ran under 2 ticks a second from per-tile water zones; figures fell through decks and posts with no colliders; the player was left behind after the Morning Check so the island showed empty sky; the attract bot kept closing Settings on touch-only devices. | The bot playing New Stay to the credits on three seeds, with the balance table beside it: bot, human-ish, shaky and idle scores per event. It showed six events giving 1000 to anyone. | Native capture timings on a machine shared with other agents (load 39 on 32 cores): they said nothing about rendering cost.\n   - Engine Feedback: Everything runs headless and the same sim plays in tests, tools and the browser. A bot playing the whole game in seconds changed how I worked. Room files plus hand-written JSON props made nine sets cheap. | Yes. A water zone per tile looked harmless but cost almost the whole frame, through merge_zones and a wave grid per rectangle. Room cameras override cues set in the same frame, so I dropped them. pav load dropped a scene's first cue. Props with no solid parts silently have no collider, which sank my figures. I also guessed the AiDef form and several prop schema rules. | The UI as data built in the sim (a node list at virtual 1080p drawn by egui), with menus as data, so pad, keys, mouse, tests and the bot share one path. Next, the Balance Core and the sequencer with its song clock. | Multiple sets in one sim. The engine assumes one room or a streaming world, so the sets, the camera per state, culling the other sets and event-placed figures all needed care. pav_app's frame function is long, and game modes thread through it as flags. | input.rs (lean, any, ui, song_pos, new buttons); frame.rs (status, fit UI, camera yaw, new events); games/mod.rs (frozen, page status, ui frame, camera yaw, extra objects); sim.rs (frozen ticks, show only the current room); puppet.rs (whole-figure tilt); parts.rs (Handle); pav_audio (buses, formants, LFO, sequencer, song clock); pav_view (BigSplash, Wake, Confetti); pav_app (fit input layout, lean shaping, weblink, hub ghosts); pav_tools (t_input lean, cue fix on load); world.rs (only_current); course.rs (no engine splash when a game places its figures). | A first-class set or stage concept: several rooms on one sim, only the current one simulated at full cost and drawn, each with its own camera and view, switched with one call. Most of my integration work was reinventing that.\n   - Prompt Feedback: The plan was specific where it mattered, with verified recipes for the hard seams: the hub block, the controller stub, the sound patch and the build times. It let me spend my effort on the game rather than on finding out how. | Little. The brief says the plan's section numbers map to its items, and the plan says the brief wins on names, so the two read together well. Whether arrow keys should both walk and step needed a decision. | Judging feel with no hands: tuning how a lean, a squat or a splash feels from bots, numbers and contact sheets. I wrote a human-like player to stand in, but nobody has held the pad or heard the sound. | Allow a final pass by a person or an instruction to report feel as untested. I would also add that a shared machine may run far slower than the plan's measured ticks per second, so browser tests should have a fast mode from the start.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - `/goal` \"Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says. Done when: Everything in PLAN.md that can be done on this computer is done, and everything TASK.md asks you to hand in is in this folder.\"\n   - Stop hook feedback (harness, on the goal condition), round 1: transcript recent window never showed STAGE/PLAN/TASK read; open items named: engine/.git left in place, native desktop build never run, hand-ins not verified per deliverable.\n   - Stop hook feedback, round 2: open items said: no person played or heard it, native window never played (only a 40-second boot), engine/.git left, 119 count combined a full run with 5 failures and a browser-only rerun, single-HTML standalone not confirmed, title not reconfirmed after last build.\n   - Stop hook feedback, round 3 (latest): \"The transcript does not show that the stop condition holds. The last message says everything is done, but the earlier evidence leaves gaps. (1) The hub ready-timing fallback was a deliberate departure from PLAN.md's script, so the plan was not followed exactly. (2) The About text and the hand-ins were audited on disk, but the 1080p screenshots of the later About pages timed out and were not confirmed. (3) PLAN.md was never quoted in the transcript, so its full requirements cannot be checked line by line against the work, and the claim that every buildable item is done rests on the assistant's own audit. (4) Items the plan requires that depend on people (playtesting, listening) remain unverified. Read in full, the transcript supports substantial completion but does not clearly show that every buildable PLAN.md requirement is satisfied.\" It then required this text-only summary.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Satisfy the Stop hook's remaining points where possible on this computer:\n     - Confirm the later About pages at 1080p on the final build (`mkdir -p engine/out`, run `tests/look.py` in the background with a long timeout, or reduce it to fewer pages; delete `engine/out` and `tests/__pycache__` afterwards).\n     - Re-read PLAN.md and write a section-by-section checklist with evidence (for example `notes/plan-audit.md`), quoting each requirement and where it is met, and noting honest differences.\n     - Address the ready fallback plainly: the plan's block failed the harness intermittently under load, so it was changed and recorded per PLAN section 0 (\"Gaps: ... decide, write one line in notes/decisions.md\") and \"change it only if it fails in play\". Do not claim the plan's script was followed exactly.\n     - People-dependent items stay unverified and are stated as such; TASK.md says they're \"never required\".\n   - Then give the final reply containing Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback (section 5 above), with honest numbers (126 passed, 0 failed).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   The final build and cleanup were complete and the last reply reported finished status. The Stop hook then returned round 3 feedback listing the four gaps above. No files changed after that feedback. State on disk: final page 03:41, `exit-interview.json` 03:37, `notes/last_test_run.txt` showing 126 passed, 0 failed; `engine/target`, `engine/out`, `engine/.git` absent; `PROGRESS.md` says \"Done... Only the final reply remained.\"\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Continue the active goal by closing what can be closed on this computer. The latest feedback says: \"the 1080p screenshots of the later About pages timed out and were not confirmed\" and \"PLAN.md was never quoted in the transcript, so its full requirements cannot be checked line by line against the work\". So: re-read PLAN.md, write the section-by-section evidence checklist to `notes/plan-audit.md`, fix any real gap it reveals (a code fix would need a rebuild and a fresh `tests/run.sh all` in one run), run `tests/look.py` in the background with a longer timeout to confirm the later About pages on the final page, clean up again, update `PROGRESS.md`, and give the final reply with the required blocks, stating the ready-fallback departure and the people-dependent items plainly.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /home/micha/.claude/projects/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-build-v2--20261104-223859--x35112d-work/0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"15887abb-da08-4b9b-996e-c541d260acd7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:10:19.785Z","isSynthetic":true}
