{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EDLpXNS6h8btATG8AQvYte","type":"tool_result","content":"506\t**Rust and JS link, no new dependencies (verified compiling and running):**\n507\t```rust\n508\tuse web_sys::js_sys::{Array, Reflect};\n509\tuse web_sys::wasm_bindgen::{JsCast, JsValue};\n510\tlet win = web_sys::window().unwrap();\n511\tReflect::set(&win, &JsValue::from_str(\"__gameStatus\"), &JsValue::from_str(&status)).ok();\n512\tlet v = Reflect::get(&win, &JsValue::from_str(\"__hub\")).unwrap_or(JsValue::UNDEFINED);\n513\t// Array::from(&v) makes a copy, so clearing it leaves the original full (verified).\n514\t// To read and clear a JS array in place: let arr: Array = v.unchecked_into(); ... arr.set_length(0);\n515\t```\n516\t`pack_single_html.py` refuses wasm-bindgen snippets (`inline_js`, `module`), so use `Reflect`. Do not use `host.exec` or `host.query` per frame: in the browser they re-publish a frame and rotate prev/curr, which stutters the interpolation. Read `curr.hud.status` instead. `Settings::load` should read `window.__gameBoot.scene` and `.seed` when present.\n517\t\n518\t**About text stays in plain text in the page.** Put it in `<script id=\"about-data\" type=\"application/json\">` in the `<head>`, not in the wasm. The agent that imports the game edits the Usage line later, and it cannot edit text inside a gzipped wasm. Rust reads it from `__gameBoot.about`.\n519\t\n520\t## 15. Verified facts and traps\n521\t\n522\tBuild times with `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8`:\n523\t- `cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav`: 1m53 first time, 15 to 70 s after. Run from `engine/`.\n524\t- `cargo test --locked -p pav_core --test games`: about 75 s build, under 1 s run.\n525\t- `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene fit --title \"...\" --out <path>`: 2m24 first time, 52 s after. Output about 11.4 MB. The wasm target and `wasm-bindgen 0.2.129` are ready. `--out` takes your brief's file name.\n526\t- `pav capture ... width=1920 height=1080`: about 0.5 s. `pav play bot=true seeds=5`: under 1 s.\n527\t- Batch Rust edits and keep numbers in TOML.\n528\t\n529\tBrowser:\n530\t- **Software rendering is slow, so size the window to the test.** Measured ticks per second: 1280x720 gives 12, 640x360 gives 42, 320x180 gives 60. Run browser tests at 320x180; only then does a 10-second attract timer take 10 seconds. Slow rendering at large sizes is not a game bug.\n531\t- Chromium flags that work: `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`. The set with `--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader` also works. Only Chromium has WebGPU here: Firefox and WebKit show the page's no-WebGPU message.\n532\t- Run your own Playwright scripts with plain `python3`. `python3 -I` cannot import Playwright here (verified).\n533\t- **Server port through a pipe:** `python3 -m http.server 0` buffers its \"port\" line when piped, and a script reading it hangs forever. Use `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory <dir>`. Stop only that PID, from a `finally` and a SIGTERM handler.\n534\t- **Controller stub (verified: gilrs reads it, stick moves the player, Cross registers):**\n535\t```js\n536\tconst btn = () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 });\n537\tconst pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 1,\n538\t              axes: [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons: Array.from({ length: 17 }, btn) };\n539\tnavigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null];\n540\twindow.__setPad = (axes, pressed) => { pad.axes = axes; pad.timestamp++; pad.buttons.forEach((b, i) => { const on = pressed.includes(i); b.pressed = on; b.touched = on; b.value = on ? 1 : 0; }); };\n541\t```\n542\t- **Measuring sound (verified):** cpal plays `AudioBufferSourceNode`s, so patch `AudioBufferSourceNode.prototype.start` in an init script, read `this.buffer.getChannelData(0)`, and accumulate RMS and peak. Sample rate 48000; context `running` after a click.\n543\t\n544\tEngine:\n545\t- `egui::Context::set_fonts` takes effect next pass; using a font family in the same pass panics \"not bound to any fonts\". Install fonts before the first `run_ui`, in `App::new` and in `Headless::frame`, which makes a new context per frame. In the browser that panic stopped the frame loop with nothing on the page to say so: `__gameStatus` simply stopped changing (verified). Log console errors and assert that the tick advances in every browser test.\n546\t- **Blob colour** is `shirt`. **Rounded legend tiles** make stripes. **Default water** is a strong blue until the zone has a `color`.\n547\t- **Mirror view is yaw 0.** The default figure faces +Z, toward a yaw-0 camera. A room `[camera]` of yaw 180 shows its back (verified).\n548\t- **Horizon lines:** full-scene outlines draw a dark line at the sea's edge; `outlines_on = \"objects\"` removes it (verified).\n549\t- **Standing on water without swimming (verified):** floor blocks with top at `-0.06` inside a water zone with `y1 = 0`. Posture stays `stand`, `swimming` false.\n550\t- `pav assets find=` appends to `store/misses.tsv`. Harmless.\n551\t- Run only your own test targets. The engine's other suites check its own catalogue and docs, and a new prop will fail its index check. You do not need them.\n552\t\n553\tHub:\n554\t- Use the exact client text; the hub's check compares it with released versions.\n555\t- The harness's Enter key test applies only to a game's own card. With the hub's card there is no key test.\n556\t\n557\t## 16. Testing\n558\t\n559\tOne command: `tests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]`. It prints only failures and a final line like `212 passed, 0 failed`. Rerun a part only after changing code it covers. Keep a running count in `notes/feedback.md` of issues found and how bad, so your testing feedback is honest.\n560\t\n561\t**`core` (`cargo test -q --locked -p pav_core --test fit`, then `cargo test -q --locked -p pav_audio -p pav_ui`; seconds to run once built):**\n562\t- The bot plays New Stay to credits on 3 seeds: outcome Won, 5 stamps, every event played, under 60 sim-minutes.\n563\t- Each event: the bot earns at least 2 stars on 5 seeds; idle input earns under 1 star; a careless random input earns less than the bot.\n564\t- Balance Core: settle time, tip after `tip_time`, keyboard ramp, stick curve.\n565\t- Morning Check: better input gives a lower age; bounds hold.\n566\t- Attract: starts at 600 idle ticks, cycles all events, any input exits, saves nothing.\n567\t- Pause freezes the world. Settings: music defaults to 0.10. Dev sliders change values and reset. Dev jump lands where it says.\n568\t- Save round trip and version. Medley on a seed gives the same score for the same inputs. Play Together completes. Ghosts match by area.\n569\t- Snapshot, rewind and replay exactness (copy `crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\n570\t- UI: `Headless::frame` readings show the right prompts per device and glyph setting; no text under the size rule (enforce in the draw helper).\n571\t- Audio: music at 10% is 0.10 of full-scale render; every SFX and song is non-silent; speakers differ.\n572\t- Content lint: no `TODO` or placeholder text in `script.toml`, and every event has a card, rules and a bot.\n573\t\n574\t**`browser` (Playwright, one browser, 320x180, `file://`):** boots with no errors; `__gameStatus` appears; the pad stub moves focus and confirms; keyboard does the same; mouse hover moves focus and click activates, using rects the UI publishes in `window.__gameUi`; prompts switch with the device; Settings has the Xbox option; attract starts after 10 s and any input exits it; music reaches about 10% by the sound patch. Touch: Chromium with a phone and a tablet profile (it has WebGPU) must show \"Controller or keyboard required\", run attract, and respond to a Settings tap by `page.touchscreen.tap`. WebKit with an iPhone profile, which has no WebGPU here, must show the fallback message from section 11.\n575\t\n576\t**`hub`:** copy the page and `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into one served folder, open `harness.html?game=<page>&players=N&auto=1`, wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === \"true\"`, and require `window.__hubCheck.pass`. Run 2 players; 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and `scenario=host-leave`. Then a solo check like the hub's: open outside a session, press Enter and Space, expect no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` not seeded. Also byte-compare the pasted client with `hub/session.js`.\n577\t\n578\t**Second player:** the harness's copies, the only multi-player check possible on one computer. **TV:** judge 1920x1080 `pav capture`s.\n579\t\n580\t**Screenshots** only for what scripts cannot check: `pav capture` for composition, `filmstrip` and `animsheet` for motion, one 1080p sheet per set at the end. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n581\t\n582\t## 17. Build order\n583\t\n584\tEach step ends with its tests passing. Early steps close the risks first.\n585\t\n586\t1. **Setup.** Pick the title. `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall engine` (it is public). Copy the starter to `games/fit/`, register it, build `pav` and the web page, first `tests/run.sh`.\n587\t2. **Seams.** Hide the chrome, fit input layout, `lean`, fonts, `fit_ui` with a Title and a Pause, Flow state machine, `weblink`, `__gameStatus`, save, a one-event Medley stub, hub JS. Get the harness and the browser smoke green now, before content exists.\n588\t3. **First slice.** Balance Core, Puck, tilt, `studio` set, Pose Parade, event card and result, bot, one result screen in full art. Play it by bot and capture it. Tune until a ring streak feels good.\n589\t4. **Island and voice.** `hub` set and props, walking, interactables, dialogue with syllables, audio buses, Lobby Bossa, Pip, the Morning Check, Balance Age, Calendar, Clam.\n590\t5. **Events** in this order: Cannonball Cup, Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Tempo Squats, Breath Bloom, Step Party (with sequencer and rhythm clock), Morning Lap, Plank Standoff, Floatie Spin, Tray Trek.\n591\t6. **Meta.** Days, unlocks, titles, wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, absence comments, all songs and SFX.\n592\t7. **Finale and endings.** Big Stand, both endings, credits, Free Play.\n593\t8. **Shell.** Attract, Settings, Dev Mode, touch-only card, How to Play, About.\n594\t9. **Multiplayer.** Full Medley, hub ghosts in every lane, Play Together.\n595\t10. **Polish.** Write the script to full length, feel pass on every event using the sliders, extra set dressing, particles, transitions, stingers.\n596\t11. **Finish** (section 18).\n597\t\n598\t**If time runs short,** cut in this order and remove all traces, leaving no stubs: Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, Plank Standoff. The roster, day table, attract list and Schedule all read from data, so a removed event leaves no hole; move its day's minute goal down to match. Everything else is required. Nothing may ship half-working; your brief says no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n599\t\n600\t## 18. Finishing\n601\t\n602\t1. Write the exit interview your brief names. Fill every field honestly; `usage` is exactly \"added on import\". Suggested `aiHub` values: type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source `Wii Fit`, series `Wii Fit`, players `1–4`, tags from `3d`, `third-person`, `comedy`, `sports`, `versus`, `low-poly`. Check that it parses.\n603\t2. Run `tools/build.sh`: copy the exit interview into `about-data` in the page, run the single-file build with your title, description and theme colour, and write the HTML where your brief says. The About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback from that block, including the fonts' and motion libraries' credits (`engine/store/CREDITS.md`, each clip set's `credit`).\n604\t3. Run `tests/run.sh all` on the final page. Open it once from `file://` at 1920x1080 and look at one frame.\n605\t4. Put the same Source Information and feedback in your chat reply.\n606\t5. Delete `engine/target` and other caches. Leave the source, tests and notes in the dev folder.\n607\t\n608\t### What each brief item maps to\n609\t\n610\t| Brief item | Section |\n611\t|---|---|\n612\t| Genre and perspective | 1 |\n613\t| Title method | 0, 17 |\n614\t| Research | Optional. The plan already reflects a short web search on Wii Fit, and that is enough; report what you actually did |\n615\t| Single HTML package | 14, 15, 18 (no external dependencies are needed) |\n616\t| Build on the engine, change anything | 14 |\n617\t| Art direction, new assets, library for generics | 8 |\n618\t| Animation | 9 |\n619\t| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | 10, 16 |\n620\t| Online and multiplayer, in the hub and on its own | 13, 16 |\n621\t| Dev folder, bundling, shared machine, ports and processes | 0, 15, 16; your brief has the rules |\n622\t| Performance out of scope, as much detail as the scene needs | 8, 15 |\n623\t| One test command, scripted playthrough, screenshots only when needed, no review agents | 16 |\n624\t| Stand-ins: pad, touch, sound, second player, iPhone, TV | 15, 16 |\n625\t| Original game, feature-complete vertical slice, extendable with normal tools | 1, 14 (all data in TOML, JSON clips and props; `README.md` explains adding an event, a set and a song) |\n626\t| Dev mode from pause, live sliders, reset | 11 |\n627\t| Attract mode | 12 |\n628\t| Narrative tone | 7 |\n629\t| 10-foot, controller-first, native keyboard and mouse, glyphs, Xbox option, no dense screens | 3, 11 |\n630\t| Touch-only behaviour | 11, 12 |\n631\t| No TODOs or stubs | 16, 17 |\n632\t| Source Information and all feedback in chat and on About, exit interview | 11, 14, 18 |\n633\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"370811fb-af9a-4919-94e0-6b80d59232f8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:10:22.837Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build-v2__20261104-223859__x35112d/work/PLAN.md","content":"**Rust and JS link, no new dependencies (verified compiling and running):**\n```rust\nuse web_sys::js_sys::{Array, Reflect};\nuse web_sys::wasm_bindgen::{JsCast, JsValue};\nlet win = web_sys::window().unwrap();\nReflect::set(&win, &JsValue::from_str(\"__gameStatus\"), &JsValue::from_str(&status)).ok();\nlet v = Reflect::get(&win, &JsValue::from_str(\"__hub\")).unwrap_or(JsValue::UNDEFINED);\n// Array::from(&v) makes a copy, so clearing it leaves the original full (verified).\n// To read and clear a JS array in place: let arr: Array = v.unchecked_into(); ... arr.set_length(0);\n```\n`pack_single_html.py` refuses wasm-bindgen snippets (`inline_js`, `module`), so use `Reflect`. Do not use `host.exec` or `host.query` per frame: in the browser they re-publish a frame and rotate prev/curr, which stutters the interpolation. Read `curr.hud.status` instead. `Settings::load` should read `window.__gameBoot.scene` and `.seed` when present.\n\n**About text stays in plain text in the page.** Put it in `<script id=\"about-data\" type=\"application/json\">` in the `<head>`, not in the wasm. The agent that imports the game edits the Usage line later, and it cannot edit text inside a gzipped wasm. Rust reads it from `__gameBoot.about`.\n\n## 15. Verified facts and traps\n\nBuild times with `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=8`:\n- `cargo build --locked -p pav_tools --bin pav`: 1m53 first time, 15 to 70 s after. Run from `engine/`.\n- `cargo test --locked -p pav_core --test games`: about 75 s build, under 1 s run.\n- `scripts/build-web.sh --single-file --scene fit --title \"...\" --out <path>`: 2m24 first time, 52 s after. Output about 11.4 MB. The wasm target and `wasm-bindgen 0.2.129` are ready. `--out` takes your brief's file name.\n- `pav capture ... width=1920 height=1080`: about 0.5 s. `pav play bot=true seeds=5`: under 1 s.\n- Batch Rust edits and keep numbers in TOML.\n\nBrowser:\n- **Software rendering is slow, so size the window to the test.** Measured ticks per second: 1280x720 gives 12, 640x360 gives 42, 320x180 gives 60. Run browser tests at 320x180; only then does a 10-second attract timer take 10 seconds. Slow rendering at large sizes is not a game bug.\n- Chromium flags that work: `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader`. The set with `--use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader` also works. Only Chromium has WebGPU here: Firefox and WebKit show the page's no-WebGPU message.\n- Run your own Playwright scripts with plain `python3`. `python3 -I` cannot import Playwright here (verified).\n- **Server port through a pipe:** `python3 -m http.server 0` buffers its \"port\" line when piped, and a script reading it hangs forever. Use `python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory <dir>`. Stop only that PID, from a `finally` and a SIGTERM handler.\n- **Controller stub (verified: gilrs reads it, stick moves the player, Cross registers):**\n```js\nconst btn = () => ({ pressed: false, touched: false, value: 0 });\nconst pad = { id: 'DualSense Wireless Controller (STANDARD GAMEPAD)', index: 0, connected: true, mapping: 'standard', timestamp: 1,\n              axes: [0, 0, 0, 0], buttons: Array.from({ length: 17 }, btn) };\nnavigator.getGamepads = () => [pad, null, null, null];\nwindow.__setPad = (axes, pressed) => { pad.axes = axes; pad.timestamp++; pad.buttons.forEach((b, i) => { const on = pressed.includes(i); b.pressed = on; b.touched = on; b.value = on ? 1 : 0; }); };\n```\n- **Measuring sound (verified):** cpal plays `AudioBufferSourceNode`s, so patch `AudioBufferSourceNode.prototype.start` in an init script, read `this.buffer.getChannelData(0)`, and accumulate RMS and peak. Sample rate 48000; context `running` after a click.\n\nEngine:\n- `egui::Context::set_fonts` takes effect next pass; using a font family in the same pass panics \"not bound to any fonts\". Install fonts before the first `run_ui`, in `App::new` and in `Headless::frame`, which makes a new context per frame. In the browser that panic stopped the frame loop with nothing on the page to say so: `__gameStatus` simply stopped changing (verified). Log console errors and assert that the tick advances in every browser test.\n- **Blob colour** is `shirt`. **Rounded legend tiles** make stripes. **Default water** is a strong blue until the zone has a `color`.\n- **Mirror view is yaw 0.** The default figure faces +Z, toward a yaw-0 camera. A room `[camera]` of yaw 180 shows its back (verified).\n- **Horizon lines:** full-scene outlines draw a dark line at the sea's edge; `outlines_on = \"objects\"` removes it (verified).\n- **Standing on water without swimming (verified):** floor blocks with top at `-0.06` inside a water zone with `y1 = 0`. Posture stays `stand`, `swimming` false.\n- `pav assets find=` appends to `store/misses.tsv`. Harmless.\n- Run only your own test targets. The engine's other suites check its own catalogue and docs, and a new prop will fail its index check. You do not need them.\n\nHub:\n- Use the exact client text; the hub's check compares it with released versions.\n- The harness's Enter key test applies only to a game's own card. With the hub's card there is no key test.\n\n## 16. Testing\n\nOne command: `tests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]`. It prints only failures and a final line like `212 passed, 0 failed`. Rerun a part only after changing code it covers. Keep a running count in `notes/feedback.md` of issues found and how bad, so your testing feedback is honest.\n\n**`core` (`cargo test -q --locked -p pav_core --test fit`, then `cargo test -q --locked -p pav_audio -p pav_ui`; seconds to run once built):**\n- The bot plays New Stay to credits on 3 seeds: outcome Won, 5 stamps, every event played, under 60 sim-minutes.\n- Each event: the bot earns at least 2 stars on 5 seeds; idle input earns under 1 star; a careless random input earns less than the bot.\n- Balance Core: settle time, tip after `tip_time`, keyboard ramp, stick curve.\n- Morning Check: better input gives a lower age; bounds hold.\n- Attract: starts at 600 idle ticks, cycles all events, any input exits, saves nothing.\n- Pause freezes the world. Settings: music defaults to 0.10. Dev sliders change values and reset. Dev jump lands where it says.\n- Save round trip and version. Medley on a seed gives the same score for the same inputs. Play Together completes. Ghosts match by area.\n- Snapshot, rewind and replay exactness (copy `crates/pav_core/tests/games.rs`).\n- UI: `Headless::frame` readings show the right prompts per device and glyph setting; no text under the size rule (enforce in the draw helper).\n- Audio: music at 10% is 0.10 of full-scale render; every SFX and song is non-silent; speakers differ.\n- Content lint: no `TODO` or placeholder text in `script.toml`, and every event has a card, rules and a bot.\n\n**`browser` (Playwright, one browser, 320x180, `file://`):** boots with no errors; `__gameStatus` appears; the pad stub moves focus and confirms; keyboard does the same; mouse hover moves focus and click activates, using rects the UI publishes in `window.__gameUi`; prompts switch with the device; Settings has the Xbox option; attract starts after 10 s and any input exits it; music reaches about 10% by the sound patch. Touch: Chromium with a phone and a tablet profile (it has WebGPU) must show \"Controller or keyboard required\", run attract, and respond to a Settings tap by `page.touchscreen.tap`. WebKit with an iPhone profile, which has no WebGPU here, must show the fallback message from section 11.\n\n**`hub`:** copy the page and `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` into one served folder, open `harness.html?game=<page>&players=N&auto=1`, wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === \"true\"`, and require `window.__hubCheck.pass`. Run 2 players; 3 and 4 players with `latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5`; and `scenario=host-leave`. Then a solo check like the hub's: open outside a session, press Enter and Space, expect no errors, `AIHub.active` false, and `Math.random` not seeded. Also byte-compare the pasted client with `hub/session.js`.\n\n**Second player:** the harness's copies, the only multi-player check possible on one computer. **TV:** judge 1920x1080 `pav capture`s.\n\n**Screenshots** only for what scripts cannot check: `pav capture` for composition, `filmstrip` and `animsheet` for motion, one 1080p sheet per set at the end. Do not use subagents or workflows to debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n## 17. Build order\n\nEach step ends with its tests passing. Early steps close the risks first.\n\n1. **Setup.** Pick the title. `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall engine` (it is public). Copy the starter to `games/fit/`, register it, build `pav` and the web page, first `tests/run.sh`.\n2. **Seams.** Hide the chrome, fit input layout, `lean`, fonts, `fit_ui` with a Title and a Pause, Flow state machine, `weblink`, `__gameStatus`, save, a one-event Medley stub, hub JS. Get the harness and the browser smoke green now, before content exists.\n3. **First slice.** Balance Core, Puck, tilt, `studio` set, Pose Parade, event card and result, bot, one result screen in full art. Play it by bot and capture it. Tune until a ring streak feels good.\n4. **Island and voice.** `hub` set and props, walking, interactables, dialogue with syllables, audio buses, Lobby Bossa, Pip, the Morning Check, Balance Age, Calendar, Clam.\n5. **Events** in this order: Cannonball Cup, Paddle Slalom, Tide Table, Tempo Squats, Breath Bloom, Step Party (with sequencer and rhythm clock), Morning Lap, Plank Standoff, Floatie Spin, Tray Trek.\n6. **Meta.** Days, unlocks, titles, wardrobe, flip-flops, Yesterday You, absence comments, all songs and SFX.\n7. **Finale and endings.** Big Stand, both endings, credits, Free Play.\n8. **Shell.** Attract, Settings, Dev Mode, touch-only card, How to Play, About.\n9. **Multiplayer.** Full Medley, hub ghosts in every lane, Play Together.\n10. **Polish.** Write the script to full length, feel pass on every event using the sliders, extra set dressing, particles, transitions, stingers.\n11. **Finish** (section 18).\n\n**If time runs short,** cut in this order and remove all traces, leaving no stubs: Tray Trek, Floatie Spin, Plank Standoff. The roster, day table, attract list and Schedule all read from data, so a removed event leaves no hole; move its day's minute goal down to match. Everything else is required. Nothing may ship half-working; your brief says no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n\n## 18. Finishing\n\n1. Write the exit interview your brief names. Fill every field honestly; `usage` is exactly \"added on import\". Suggested `aiHub` values: type `Game`, genre `Sports`, source `Wii Fit`, series `Wii Fit`, players `1–4`, tags from `3d`, `third-person`, `comedy`, `sports`, `versus`, `low-poly`. Check that it parses.\n2. Run `tools/build.sh`: copy the exit interview into `about-data` in the page, run the single-file build with your title, description and theme colour, and write the HTML where your brief says. The About screen shows Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback from that block, including the fonts' and motion libraries' credits (`engine/store/CREDITS.md`, each clip set's `credit`).\n3. Run `tests/run.sh all` on the final page. Open it once from `file://` at 1920x1080 and look at one frame.\n4. Put the same Source Information and feedback in your chat reply.\n5. Delete `engine/target` and other caches. Leave the source, tests and notes in the dev folder.\n\n### What each brief item maps to\n\n| Brief item | Section |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective | 1 |\n| Title method | 0, 17 |\n| Research | Optional. The plan already reflects a short web search on Wii Fit, and that is enough; report what you actually did |\n| Single HTML package | 14, 15, 18 (no external dependencies are needed) |\n| Build on the engine, change anything | 14 |\n| Art direction, new assets, library for generics | 8 |\n| Animation | 9 |\n| Audio in code, gibberish voices, music at 10% | 10, 16 |\n| Online and multiplayer, in the hub and on its own | 13, 16 |\n| Dev folder, bundling, shared machine, ports and processes | 0, 15, 16; your brief has the rules |\n| Performance out of scope, as much detail as the scene needs | 8, 15 |\n| One test command, scripted playthrough, screenshots only when needed, no review agents | 16 |\n| Stand-ins: pad, touch, sound, second player, iPhone, TV | 15, 16 |\n| Original game, feature-complete vertical slice, extendable with normal tools | 1, 14 (all data in TOML, JSON clips and props; `README.md` explains adding an event, a set and a song) |\n| Dev mode from pause, live sliders, reset | 11 |\n| Attract mode | 12 |\n| Narrative tone | 7 |\n| 10-foot, controller-first, native keyboard and mouse, glyphs, Xbox option, no dense screens | 3, 11 |\n| Touch-only behaviour | 11, 12 |\n| No TODOs or stubs | 16, 17 |\n| Source Information and all feedback in chat and on About, exit interview | 11, 14, 18 |\n","numLines":128,"startLine":506,"totalLines":633}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EDLpXNS6h8btATG8AQvYte","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
