gine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/core.rs\n   131 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/dialog.rs\n   220 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/finale.rs\n  1953 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/flow.rs\n   128 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/ghost.rs\n   100 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/island.rs\n   310 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/medley.rs\n   128 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/menus.rs\n   218 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/meta.rs\n   576 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/mod.rs\n   329 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/rules.rs\n   285 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/run.rs\n   882 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/screens.rs\n    87 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/script.rs\n   318 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/ui_model.rs\n   365 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/world.rs\n   163 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/breath.rs\n   273 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/dive.rs\n   318 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/lap.rs\n   439 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/mod.rs\n   218 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/paddle.rs\n   157 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/plank.rs\n   170 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/pose.rs\n   237 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/spin.rs\n   147 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/squats.rs\n   287 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/step.rs\n   285 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/tide.rs\n   274 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/events/tray.rs\n    50 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/charts.toml\n   230 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/rules.toml\n   425 engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/script.toml\n 10309 total\n---\n# Decisions the plan left open\n- Title: Whiff Fit, one of 50 brainstormed, picked with Python's `secrets`.\n- Sets have no `[camera]`: every camera comes from cues, because a room camera applied in the same frame as a cue overrode it.\n- All game logic runs in `Game::pre`; `post` only filters the character's own Land/Jump/Splash events, since events place figures by hand.\n- One water zone per set (three for the channel), not one per tile: `merge_zones` per tile and grid per zone cost 98% of the frame.\n- Frames show only the current set (`World.only_current`), and rewind history is off in the game (the test turns it on).\n- The Commodore on the island is a prop on a mooring post (with his mark as the talk spot); flying gulls are the three-entity rigs.\n- Judges are gull props on a raft; the score cards are UI, big enough for 10 feet.\n- Tray Trek's glasses keep sliding until tilted back (no spring to the centre), so idle input loses them. Score 180 per glass plus 100 no-spill (plan said 200 plus a bonus, capped at 1000).\n- Breath Bloom's ring only counts while the breath is near the guide; Tempo Squats only credits reps you went down for; otherwise doing nothing earned a star.\n- Morning Lap ends itself at 130 s so an idle player isn't stuck; Paddle Slalom likewise at 110 s.\n- The wardrobe opens only from the island (it needs the camera and the figure); the mat at the pier and the Schedule both start the Big Stand.\n- Sleep needs the day's goal; repeats always bank one minute, so nobody is ever stuck.\n- Settings gains a Back row on touch-only devices, since a finger has no Back button.\n- Tests run with `?fast=1` (no shadows or ripples): on a shared software-rendered machine the page otherwise ran under 2 ticks a second.\n- Attract's 10-second timer runs on the title, the pre-game menus and Settings over them, but not on About or How to Play: those are pages to read, and a demo starting mid-sentence would be rude.\n- In a session the page says ready at its first status, or 12 s after connecting once the canvas exists, whichever is first. The plan's block waited only for the status; on a software renderer under heavy load a copy could spend over 20 s (once over 200 s) inside `popErrorScope` while pipelines compiled, and the protocol sits such a player out. The game joins the round at its first frame.\n- Attract adds Breath Bloom and Tempo Squats to section 12's list, because section 5 gives every event an attract segment.\n- The Schedule is a column of big rows rather than a sideways carousel: it holds six items, shows stars and subtitles at 10 feet, and moves the same way as every other menu.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"dda052ea-73ba-4090-a08d-27452895f8ea","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:10:34.171Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".:\ntotal 32\ndrwxr-xr-x  7 micha micha 4096 Nov  5 01:07 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  3 micha micha 4096 Nov  5 01:06 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 micha micha 2787 Nov  5 04:06 README.md\ndrwxr-xr-x 15 micha micha 4096 Nov  5 04:06 engine\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 micha micha 4096 Nov  4 22:39 hub\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 micha micha 4096 Nov  5 02:38 notes\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 micha micha 4096 Nov  5 04:06 tests\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 micha micha 4096 Nov  5 00:51 tools\n\nhub:\ntotal 112\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  4 22:39 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 micha micha  4096 Nov  5 01:07 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 17587 Nov  4 22:39 README.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 13624 Nov  4 22:39 bridge.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 27469 Nov  4 22:39 harness.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 20248 Nov  4 22:39 round.js\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 16707 Nov  4 22:39 session.js\n\nnotes:\ntotal 104\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  5 02:38 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 micha micha  4096 Nov  5 01:07 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   573 Nov  4 23:38 credits.txt\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  2627 Nov  5 02:19 decisions.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 78176 Nov  5 04:06 engine.diff\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  3835 Nov  5 03:37 feedback.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha   351 Nov  5 04:06 last_test_run.txt\n\ntests:\ntotal 44\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  5 04:06 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 7 micha micha  4096 Nov  5 01:07 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha  1097 Nov  5