{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BAcAPBurN2uy1gN6ofo94v","type":"tool_result","content":"engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/screens.rs:569:        ui.prompt_row(&[(Act::Menu, \"Choose\"), (Act::Confirm, \"Confirm\")]);\nengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/screens.rs:821:                let mut prompts: Vec<(Act, &str)> = vec![(Act::Menu, \"Choose\")\nengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/screens.rs:853:                ui.prompt_row_at(1040.0, &[(Act::Menu, \"Choose\"), (Act::Confir\nengine/crates/pav_ui/src/glyphs.rs:71:            Act::Menu => G::Dpad,\nengine/crates/pav_ui/src/glyphs.rs:132:                Act::Menu => G::Key(\"W S\"),\n15:43-    Menu,\n---\n# Whiff Fit: how this folder works\n\nA five-day balance comedy at a resort staffed by talking gym equipment, built on the Pavilion\nengine (Shardfall, from commit 49ef2ba; `notes/engine.diff` holds the changes to its existing files). `PLAN.md` in the parent folder is the design this was built from.\n\n## Layout\n- `engine/`: the engine, with the game in `crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/`:\n  - `mod.rs` the `FitGame` state, `flow.rs` what each screen does in a tick, `screens.rs` every menu\n    and screen as data, `run.rs` card/3-2-1/play/result, `events/*.rs` one file per event,\n    `check.rs` the morning test, `finale.rs` the Big Stand, `medley.rs` the Medley,\n    `meta.rs` saves and wardrobe, `bot.rs` the bot that plays it all.\n  - Data: `rules.toml` (every number), `script.toml` (all the words), `charts.toml` (Step Party),\n    `sets/*.toml` (one room per set).\n  - `crates/pav_ui/src/fit_ui.rs` draws the UI the sim describes; `crates/pav_audio/src/music.rs` and\n    `voice.rs` are the songs and gibberish; `crates/pav_app/src/weblink.rs` joins the game and its page.\n- `tools/`: `make_props.py`, `make_sets.py`, `make_clips.py` write the JSON props, TOML sets and\n  `anim/fit.json`; `build.sh` builds the one-file page; `tour.py`, `shots.sh` take captures.\n- `tests/run.sh [core|browser|hub|all]`: the one test command. Prints failures and a count. `tests/look.py` takes 1080p screenshots of the finished page; `tests/boot_time\n- `hub/`: the AI Hub client and harness, as downloaded.\n- `notes/`: decisions, testing feedback, credits.\n\nRunning from `engine/`, `pav` reads `rules.toml`, `script.toml`, `charts.toml` and the sets from\ndisk at every `load`, so changing them needs no rebuild: `./target/debug/pav play scene=fit bot=true`.\nThe browser build embeds them. Add `?fast=1` to the page to skip shadows and ripples on software renderers.\n\n## Add an event\n1. Copy `events/breath.rs`; give it `start`, `tick` (returns `Some(score)` at the end), `stop`, `hud`, `bot`.\n2. Add a line each to `EventKind` (key, name, coach, opening day, set, lane), `ALL`, `EventState` and its `each!` macro, in `events/mod.rs`.\n3. Add it to a pavilion in `island.rs`, `card.<key>` lines in `script.toml`, a group in `rules.rs` and `rules.toml`.\n4. `tests/fit.rs` then requires its bot to earn 2 stars and idle input to earn none. Add it to `ATTRACT` in `flow.rs`.\n\n## Add a set\nAdd a function to `tools/make_sets.py` (or write `sets/<name>.toml` by hand: a `stage` marker, `[view]`, objects), add it to `Set` and `SETS` in `world.rs`.\n\n## Add a song\nWrite a function in `pav_audio/src/music.rs` (tracks of a patch and a pattern of scale degrees over a chord progression), add it to `song()`, a constant in `world.rs`'s `\n---\n# Running count of issues found by testing (plan section 16)\n\nCritical (game breaking):\n1. Under 2 ticks a second in the browser: one water zone per tile, merged every frame, each with its own wave grid. Fixed with one zone per set and drawing only the curre\n2. Figures fell through decks, posts and rafts that had no colliders (Studio, Bay, Pier): the captures showed heads at floor level.\n3. After the Morning Check the player stayed in the Studio while the island drew around nothing: an empty sky.\n4. Touch-only attract: the bot pressed Back on the touch card every few ticks, closing Settings at once and playing no event.\n\nSerious:\n5. First pointer move had delta 0, so hover did not move focus until the second move.\n6. Keys with no binding did not count as \"any input\", so they did not leave attract.\n7. A finger's release lost the pointer's position, so taps missed.\n8. `pav load` dropped a scene's first camera cue (tool session bug), so captures showed the wrong camera.\n9. Click on Pip never arrived: Pip sits behind a desk. Now within reach is close enough.\n10. Walking off the land's edge dropped you in the sea: the walk limit matched the tile edge exactly.\n11. Paddle Slalom's gusts were strong enough to tip the bot (350 to 520). Gust 40 to 16.\n12. Idle play earned a star on Breath Bloom and Tempo Squats until the rules counted only real effort.\n13. Eight prop schema errors, caught by room_check (sphere arc, lathe needed, categories, ref fields).\n14. Big Stand's brace scored out of 60 s, not its 20 s, and used the gazebo's lines and a plank on a post.\n15. Character landings and water entries made sound and spray every tick events placed the figure in water.\n\nMinor:\n16. Prompt rows clipped their labels; widths are now measured where the fonts are.\n17. Calendar and Pass cards double-dimmed by the menu's fade.\n18. The base screen's prompt row showed through overlays.\n19. Morning camera sat behind the cabana; look screen stood in front of the smoothie stall.\n20. Morning Lap's ghost score text overlapped the score.\n21. Six events saturated at 1000 for a shaky human-like player until difficulty was tuned from the balance table.\n22. Tests sampled the title too late; first-frame card press was refused by the 0.2 s guard. At load 56 the stay test's pad taps could also end before any frame saw them;\n23. Reading the code found Step Party's song starting at the card, so its beat missed the notes. A test now pins it to the first tick of play. (Found by reading, then tes\n24. The harness intermittently failed \"ready without a key press\" with 3 to 4 copies under machine load: copies waited on pipeline compilation in the GPU process. Now rea\n25. A line-by-line audit of the plan after I first called this done found gaps no test had caught: three named library clips and five library props unused, three hand-key\n26. Seen on the result screen while driving the native window: \"1 minutes for the Clam\". Reading the code then found Pip's wave line shown unfilled (\"{n}th wave\"), plus \"\n\nTotal: 26 issues, 4 critical.\nMost helpful: the bot playing New Stay to credits on three seeds, plus the human-ish balance table.\nLeast helpful: native capture timing on a machine shared with other agents (load 39 on 32 cores) told me nothing about rendering cost.\n---\nnotes/last_test_run.txt\n/usr/bin/xvfb-run\n/usr/bin/Xvfb\n{\n  \"sourceInformation\": {\n    \"date\": \"2026-11-04 22:38:59\",\n    \"source\": \"Wii Fit\",\n    \"plan\": \"PLAN.md\",\n    \"genre\": \"Sports mini-game anthology with a light life-sim frame (daily ritual, unlocks, wardrobe)\",\n    \"perspective\": \"Third person, a camera per activity: 3/4 follow on the island, mirror-style front view for exercises, chase for the lap, paddle and tray, high 3/4 for the raft, side view for the d\n    \"tech\": \"Rust 1.98.1 compiled to WebAssembly with WebGPU; Pavilion engine (Shardfall repository, commit 49ef2ba, changed for this game): rapier3d 0.36 physics, wgpu renderer, egui 0.36 painter UI,\n    \"artDirection\": \"The engine's cel-shaded rounded primitives with thin ink outlines, taken high-key and pastel: 37 hand-written props, nine sets, a painted UI in Fredoka and Nunito\",\n    \"animation\": \"The engine's procedural puppet with motion clips: 25 hand-keyed clips (FIT set) plus library clips from Mesh2Motion, CMU, 100STYLE and Quaternius; poses scrubbed by gameplay; whole-f\n    \"audio\": \"All in code with no audio files: six sequenced songs (bossa, pads, waltz, funk-pop, mallets, march), 43 synthesized sound effects and stingers, Animalese-style gibberish voices from form\n    \"online\": \"AI Hub session (ghost mode, 1 to 4 players): the Inter-Resort Medley with other players as seat-coloured ghosts in neighbouring lanes. Solo: Play Together passes one pad among 2 to 4 gu\n    \"testing\": \"Headless only: Rust tests with a bot that plays New Stay to the credits, each event on five seeds, balance tables with a human-like player; Playwright in Chromium with a stub pad, keys\n    \"research\": \"None beyond the plan's own short web search on Wii Fit; I read the engine's docs and source and the AI Hub protocol\",\n    \"environment\": \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\",\n    \"model\": \"Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort xhigh\",\n    \"usage\": \"added on import\"\n  },\n  \"testingFeedback\": [\n    \"26 issues, counted in notes/feedback.md as I went.\",\n    \"4: the page ran under 2 ticks a second from per-tile water zones; figures fell through decks and posts with no colliders; the player was left behind after the Morning Check so the island showed e\n    \"The bot playing New Stay to the credits on three seeds, with the balance table beside it: bot, human-ish, shaky and idle scores per event. It showed six events giving 1000 to anyone.\",\n    \"Native capture timings on a machine shared with other agents (load 39 on 32 cores): they said nothing about rendering cost.\"\n  ],\n  \"engineFeedback\": [\n    \"Everything runs headless and the same sim plays in tests, tools and the browser. A bot playing the whole game in seconds changed how I worked. Room files plus hand-written JSON props made nine se\n    \"Yes. A water zone per tile looked harmless but cost almost the whole frame, through merge_zones and a wave grid per rectangle. Room cameras override cues set in the same frame, so I dropped them.\n    \"The UI as data built in the sim (a node list at virtual 1080p drawn by egui), with menus as data, so pad, keys, mouse, tests and the bot share one path. Next, the Balance Core and the sequencer w\n    \"Multiple sets in one sim. The engine assumes one room or a streaming world, so the sets, the camera per state, culling the other sets and event-placed figures all needed care. pav_app's frame fun\n    \"input.rs (lean, any, ui, song_pos, new buttons); frame.rs (status, fit UI, camera yaw, new events); games/mod.rs (frozen, page status, ui frame, camera yaw, extra objects); sim.rs (frozen ticks, \n['sourceInformation', 'testingFeedback', 'engineFeedback', 'promptFeedback', 'aiHub']\n[\"26 issues, counted in notes/feedback.md as I went.\", \"4: the page ran under 2 ticks a second from per-tile water zones; figures fell through decks and posts with no colliders; the player was left behind after the Morning Check so the island showed empty sky; the attract bot kept closing Settings on touch-only devices.\", \"The bot playing New Stay to the credits on three seeds, with the balance table beside it: bot, human-ish, shaky and idle scores per event. It showed six events giving 1000 to anyone.\", \"Native capture timings on a machine shared with other agents (load 39 on 32 cores): they said nothing about rendering cost.\"]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0691f0d6-f08e-44c9-b7bd-c57d7fb96b71","uuid":"120afcf9-841f-463e-bc40-ed0a88b7acc8","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:35:04.389Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"engine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/screens.rs:569:        ui.prompt_row(&[(Act::Menu, \"Choose\"), (Act::Confirm, \"Confirm\")]);\nengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/screens.rs:821:                let mut prompts: Vec<(Act, &str)> = vec![(Act::Menu, \"Choose\")\nengine/crates/pav_core/src/games/fit/screens.rs:853:                ui.prompt_row_at(1040.0, &[(Act::Menu, \"Choose\"), (Act::Confir\nengine/crates/pav_ui/src/glyphs.rs:71:            Act::Menu => G::Dpad,\nengine/crates/pav_ui/src/glyphs.rs:132:                Act::Menu => G::Key(\"W S\"),\n15:43