six items, shows stars and subtitles at 10 feet, and moves the same way as every other menu.\\n\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, \"- The Schedule's carousel slides only when the focus would leave the three cards in view, rather than keeping the focus centred: a centred one moves the card under a still mouse pointer.\\n\")\nold = \"- The Commodore on the island is a prop on a mooring post (with his mark as the talk spot); flying gulls are the three-entity rigs.\\n\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, \"- The Commodore is a body on a mooring post and two wings, rotated in code, on the island and all four lagoon sets. His post is part of the body prop, because he has to stand on something.\\n\")\nold = \"- Judges are gull props on a raft; the score cards are UI, big enough for 10 feet.\\n\"\nassert old in s; s = s.replace(old, \"- Judges are gull props on a raft holding scorecard props; the numbers themselves are UI, big enough for 10 feet.\\n\")\ns = s.rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n- Step Party's chart has 125 notes in 24 bars (plan: about 100). The bot, the human-like player and the balance table all read it at that density, so it stayed.\\n- Plank Standoff's stars count seconds (25, 40, 55); every other event uses the common 400, 650, 850. Both come from the plan, and its score stays seconds out of 60.\\n- A page's boot data also carries the touch and test switches the page needs, beyond the plan's block.\\n\"\nd.write_text(s)\n# ---- the running count\nf = pathlib.Path('notes/feedback.md'); s = f.read_text()\nold = \"Total: 26 issues, 4 critical.\"\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"Found by rereading the plan line by line after I had called the game done a second time (so tests had not caught them):\n27. The Schedule was a column of rows; the plan says a carousel. I had recorded it as a decision, but it had not failed in play. Serious.\n28. Plank stars came at 24, 39 and 51 s from the common thresholds; the plan says 25, 40 and 55. Minor.\n29. On the island a comment said the thing under the pointer gets a ring. The click worked; the ring had never been drawn. Serious.\n30. The Commodore was one wingless prop on two of his five sets; the plan says three entities with wings rotated in code. Serious.\n31. Two sounds were never played (the small splash, the heartbeat), though the exit interview counted them among 43. Minor. A test now requires every sound to have a caller.\n32. No bubbles anywhere, and nobody in the background of the tower. Minor.\n33. Missing tests: only one song was checked for silence, ghosts were not checked by area, rules sections were not linted. Added.\n34. Seen when I looked at the new carousel: the keyboard prompt said W S on a menu that moves with A D. Minor.\n\nTotal: 34 issues, 4 critical.\"\"\")\nf.write_text(s)\n# ---- exit interview: same words go in the page's About\ne = pathlib.Path('../exit-interview.json'); d = json.loads(e.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))\nassert d['testingFeedback'][0].startswith('26 issues')\nd['testingFeedback'][0] = \"34 issues, counted in notes/feedback.md as I went. The last eight came from rereading the plan line by line after I had called the game done: no test had caught them.\"\ne.write_text(json.dumps(d, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2) + \"\\n\", encoding='utf-8')\nEOF\npython3 notes/.audit/patch4.py && git -C .. status --short -- . 2>/dev/null | head -0; python3 -c \"\nimport json;d=json.load(open('../exit-interview.json'));print(d['sourceInformation']['usage'], '|', d['testingFeedback'][0]); print(list(d['aiHub'])[:4])\"; mkdir -p notes/.audit/base && cd notes/.audit/base && git init -q . 2>/dev/null; git remote add origin https://github.com/michaelcrosato/shardfall 2>/dev/null; timeout 120 git fetch -q --depth 1 origin 49ef2ba 2>&1 | tail -1 | cut -c1-200; git rev-parse --short FETCH_HEAD 2>&1 | cut -c1-20","description":"Fix the prompt, update notes and exit interview, fetch the engine base","timeout":180000}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01RM9VzCLpJwXF4u5